window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/a465-21f384aaedf27d38.json"]={sha256:"21f384aaedf27d38ae82b7aa15d8bc7ea2248304f03e84226b146f56bc8d7d3b",value:{"id":"a465","title":"矽像素粒子追蹤器","titleEn":"Silicon-pixel particle trackers","category":"instruments","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以 CMS 與 ALICE 的像素追蹤器為參照，從最小游離粒子在 285 µm 矽中釋放約兩萬兩千個電子出發，把空乏與 Lorentz 偏移、混合式與 MAPS 架構、輻射損傷、位置解析度、物質量、觸發緩衝與軌跡式對準串成一份可驗收、可交接的追蹤器工程紀錄。","summaryEn":"Using the CMS and ALICE pixel trackers as references, start from the roughly 22,000 electrons a minimum-ionising particle frees in 285 µm of silicon, then connect depletion and Lorentz drift, hybrid versus MAPS architectures, radiation damage, spatial resolution, material budget, trigger buffering and track-based alignment into an acceptable, transferable tracker engineering record.","scope":"依公開物理原理與官方資料編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是原廠配方、施工圖、設備操作許可或安全程序。數值均為教學假設，需依實際規格重算。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public physics and official sources. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, operating authorisation or safety procedures. Numbers are teaching assumptions and must be recalculated for real specifications.","subcategory":"optics-accelerators-detectors","subcategoryTitle":"加速器、光束線與粒子偵測器","subcategoryTitleEn":"Accelerators, beamlines and particle detectors","learningTrack":"optics","learningSubdiscipline":"optics-accelerators-detectors","learningTags":["optics","optics-accelerators-detectors","detector"],"architectureFamily":"detector","architectureNodes":[["矽感測器（空乏二極體）","Silicon sensor (depleted diode)"],["凸塊接合與讀出晶片","Bump bonds and readout chip"],["冷卻與碳纖維支撐","Cooling and carbon-fibre support"],["觸發緩衝與資料鏈路","Trigger buffers and data links"],["軌跡重建與對準","Track reconstruction and alignment"],["偏壓與漏電流監控","Bias and leakage-current monitoring"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,3],[3,4],[2,0],[5,0],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"detector","labels":["矽感測器（空乏二極體）","凸塊接合與讀出晶片","冷卻與碳纖維支撐","觸發緩衝與資料鏈路","軌跡重建與對準"],"labelsEn":["Silicon sensor (depleted diode)","Bump bonds and readout chip","Cooling and carbon-fibre support","Trigger buffers and data links","Track reconstruction and alignment"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"內層模組設計練習：假設高亮度型內層採 50×50 µm² 像素、150 µm 厚感測器與 400×384 像素的讀出晶片。薄感測器取最可能值 72 e⁻/µm，訊號 MPV ≈ 72 × 150 = 10,800 e⁻；門檻 1,000 e⁻ 為 MPV 的 9.3%，雜訊 80 e⁻ 時門檻與雜訊比為 12.5。二元解析度 50/√12 ≈ 14.4 µm；感測器物質量 150/93,700 ≈ 0.16% X₀。未照射時 3 kΩ·cm 基材的空乏電壓按 d² 縮放為 95 × (150/285)² ≈ 26 V；照射到 Φ_eq = 2×10¹⁵ cm⁻² 後 N_eff ≈ 3×10¹³ cm⁻³，空乏電壓約 510 V。每像素體積 3.75×10⁻⁷ cm³，20 °C 漏電流 = 4×10⁻¹⁷ × 2×10¹⁵ × 3.75×10⁻⁷ = 30 nA，冷到 −15 °C 乘以 0.030 得 0.90 nA；整顆晶片 153,600 像素約 0.14 mA，500 V 偏壓下約 0.07 W。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實驗的規格。","textEn":"Inner-module design exercise: assume a high-luminosity inner layer with 50×50 µm² pixels, a 150 µm sensor and a 400×384-pixel readout chip. Taking a most probable 72 e⁻/µm for thin sensors, the signal MPV ≈ 72 × 150 = 10,800 e⁻; a 1,000 e⁻ threshold is 9.3% of the MPV, and with 80 e⁻ noise the threshold-to-noise ratio is 12.5. Binary resolution is 50/√12 ≈ 14.4 µm and sensor material is 150/93,700 ≈ 0.16% X₀. Unirradiated 3 kΩ·cm bulk depletes at 95 × (150/285)² ≈ 26 V by d² scaling; after Φ_eq = 2×10¹⁵ cm⁻², N_eff ≈ 3×10¹³ cm⁻³ and the depletion voltage is about 510 V. Each pixel has a volume of 3.75×10⁻⁷ cm³, so leakage at 20 °C is 4×10⁻¹⁷ × 2×10¹⁵ × 3.75×10⁻⁷ = 30 nA, and cooling to −15 °C multiplies by 0.030 to give 0.90 nA; the 153,600-pixel chip draws about 0.14 mA, about 0.07 W at 500 V. Values are teaching assumptions, not any experiment's specification.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變系統邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not measured hardware, product ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after changing the system boundary.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與設施背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and facility context, not these numbers."},"depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":12,"enrichmentVersion":12,"stages":[{"id":"a465-v12-s1","title":"系統邊界與物理原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and physical principles","description":"本階段聚焦「最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號」與「空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal\" and \"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a465-v12-01","title":"最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「MIP 游離軌跡與訊號電荷」如何決定矽像素粒子追蹤器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “MIP ionisation track and signal charge” determines the key performance of “Silicon-pixel particle trackers”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"帶電粒子穿過矽時以游離方式損失能量，最小游離粒子（MIP）的平均能損約 1.66 MeV·cm²/g，每產生一對電子—電洞需要 3.62 eV。少數高能 δ 電子會一次帶走大量能量，使能損分佈成為右尾很長的 Landau 分佈，最可能值只有平均值的約七成，因此門檻與信噪比必須用最可能值而非平均值設計。像素追蹤器的任務，就是在 LHC 25 ns 的束團間隔內把這數千到兩萬多個電子收集進讀出電路，並判斷它是否越過門檻。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「MIP 游離軌跡與訊號電荷」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A charged particle crossing silicon loses energy by ionisation; a minimum-ionising particle (MIP) deposits on average about 1.66 MeV·cm²/g, and each electron–hole pair costs 3.62 eV. A few energetic delta electrons occasionally carry away a large share of the energy, so the loss follows a Landau distribution with a long upper tail whose most probable value is only about 70% of the mean; thresholds and signal-to-noise must therefore be designed on the most probable value, not the mean. The pixel tracker's job is to collect these several thousand to twenty-odd thousand electrons into the readout circuit within the 25 ns LHC bunch spacing and decide whether they cross threshold. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “MIP ionisation track and signal charge”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：平均能損 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm，除以 3.62 eV 得平均約 107 對/µm；最可能值約 78 對/µm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Mean loss 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm; dividing by 3.62 eV gives about 107 pairs/µm on average, with a most probable value near 78 pairs/µm.","failure":"常見誤解：「每顆穿過像素的粒子都產生同樣多的電子，訊號是固定值。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every particle crossing a pixel frees the same number of electrons, so the signal is fixed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「MIP 游離軌跡與訊號電荷」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “MIP ionisation track and signal charge”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-01-k1","title":"最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號","titleEn":"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal","text":"帶電粒子穿過矽時以游離方式損失能量，最小游離粒子（MIP）的平均能損約 1.66 MeV·cm²/g，每產生一對電子—電洞需要 3.62 eV。少數高能 δ 電子會一次帶走大量能量，使能損分佈成為右尾很長的 Landau 分佈，最可能值只有平均值的約七成，因此門檻與信噪比必須用最可能值而非平均值設計。","textEn":"A charged particle crossing silicon loses energy by ionisation; a minimum-ionising particle (MIP) deposits on average about 1.66 MeV·cm²/g, and each electron–hole pair costs 3.62 eV. A few energetic delta electrons occasionally carry away a large share of the energy, so the loss follows a Landau distribution with a long upper tail whose most probable value is only about 70% of the mean; thresholds and signal-to-noise must therefore be designed on the most probable value, not the mean.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每顆穿過像素的粒子都產生同樣多的電子，訊號是固定值。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every particle crossing a pixel frees the same number of electrons, so the signal is fixed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal\" is correct?","options":["每顆穿過像素的粒子都產生同樣多的電子，訊號是固定值。","帶電粒子穿過矽時以游離方式損失能量，最小游離粒子（MIP）的平均能損約 1.66 MeV·cm²/g，每產生一對電子—電洞需要 3.62 eV。","只要接上偏壓，整片感測器就全部是靈敏區，空乏深度與偏壓無關。"],"optionsEn":["Every particle crossing a pixel frees the same number of electrons, so the signal is fixed.","A charged particle crossing silicon loses energy by ionisation.","Once bias is applied the whole sensor is sensitive, and depletion depth does not depend on voltage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"帶電粒子穿過矽時以游離方式損失能量，最小游離粒子（MIP）的平均能損約 1.66 MeV·cm²/g，每產生一對電子—電洞需要 3.62 eV。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A charged particle crossing silicon loses energy by ionisation; a minimum-ionising particle (MIP) deposits on average about 1.66 MeV·cm²/g, and each electron–hole pair costs 3.62 eV. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"a465-v12-02","title":"最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號：定量估算","titleEn":"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「MIP 游離軌跡與訊號電荷」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “MIP ionisation track and signal charge” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：平均能損 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm，除以 3.62 eV 得平均約 107 對/µm；最可能值約 78 對/µm。285 µm 感測器：MPV ≈ 78 × 285 ≈ 22,200 e⁻ ≈ 3.6 fC，平均值約 30,500 e⁻。若前端雜訊為 120 e⁻ ENC、門檻 1,800 e⁻，則 MPV 信噪比 ≈ 185，門檻只佔 MPV 的 8%，同時是雜訊的 15 倍。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Mean loss 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm; dividing by 3.62 eV gives about 107 pairs/µm on average, with a most probable value near 78 pairs/µm. For a 285 µm sensor the MPV ≈ 78 × 285 ≈ 22,200 e⁻ ≈ 3.6 fC, while the mean is about 30,500 e⁻. With 120 e⁻ ENC front-end noise and a 1,800 e⁻ threshold, the MPV signal-to-noise is about 185 and the threshold is only 8% of the MPV yet 15 times the noise. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以 ⁹⁰Sr β 源（高能端電子近似 MIP）或測試束照射模組，先用讀出晶片內建的校正注入電容把 ToT 或 ADC 值換成電子數，再對叢集電荷擬合 Landau 與 Gauss 的摺積求 MPV 與寬度，與 22,000 e⁻ 的預期比較；同時在無照射時掃描門檻取得每個像素的 S 曲線，由其寬度求 ENC、由其中點求實際門檻分佈。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Irradiate the module with a ⁹⁰Sr beta source, whose high-energy electrons approximate MIPs, or with a test beam; first convert ToT or ADC values into electrons with the readout chip's built-in calibration-injection capacitor, then fit a Landau convolved with a Gaussian to the cluster charge to obtain MPV and width and compare with the expected 22,000 e⁻.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"平均能損 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm，除以 3.62 eV 得平均約 107 對/µm；最可能值約 78 對/µm。285 µm 感測器：MPV ≈ 78 × 285 ≈ 22,200 e⁻ ≈ 3.6 fC，平均值約 30,500 e⁻。若前端雜訊為 120 e⁻ ENC、門檻 1,800 e⁻，則 MPV 信噪比 ≈ 185，門檻只佔 MPV 的 8%，同時是雜訊的 15 倍。","textEn":"Mean loss 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm; dividing by 3.62 eV gives about 107 pairs/µm on average, with a most probable value near 78 pairs/µm. For a 285 µm sensor the MPV ≈ 78 × 285 ≈ 22,200 e⁻ ≈ 3.6 fC, while the mean is about 30,500 e⁻. With 120 e⁻ ENC front-end noise and a 1,800 e⁻ threshold, the MPV signal-to-noise is about 185 and the threshold is only 8% of the MPV yet 15 times the noise.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal\", which statement holds?","options":["漏電流只取決於累積的輻射劑量，與運轉溫度無關。","像素越小，頂點解析度一定越好，與物質量無關。","平均能損 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm，除以 3.62 eV 得平均約 107 對/µm。"],"optionsEn":["Leakage current depends only on accumulated radiation dose, not on operating temperature.","Smaller pixels always give better vertex resolution regardless of material.","Mean loss 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均能損 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm，除以 3.62 eV 得平均約 107 對/µm；最可能值約 78 對/µm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Mean loss 1.664 MeV·cm²/g × 2.329 g/cm³ = 3.88 MeV/cm = 388 eV/µm; dividing by 3.62 eV gives about 107 pairs/µm on average, with a most probable value near 78 pairs/µm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"a465-v12-03","title":"最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「MIP 游離軌跡與訊號電荷」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “MIP ionisation track and signal charge” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以 ⁹⁰Sr β 源（高能端電子近似 MIP）或測試束照射模組，先用讀出晶片內建的校正注入電容把 ToT 或 ADC 值換成電子數，再對叢集電荷擬合 Landau 與 Gauss 的摺積求 MPV 與寬度，與 22,000 e⁻ 的預期比較；同時在無照射時掃描門檻取得每個像素的 S 曲線，由其寬度求 ENC、由其中點求實際門檻分佈。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Irradiate the module with a ⁹⁰Sr beta source, whose high-energy electrons approximate MIPs, or with a test beam; first convert ToT or ADC values into electrons with the readout chip's built-in calibration-injection capacitor, then fit a Landau convolved with a Gaussian to the cluster charge to obtain MPV and width and compare with the expected 22,000 e⁻. Without beam, scan the threshold to obtain each pixel's S-curve, taking ENC from its width and the true threshold distribution from its midpoints. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：若把平均值 30,500 e⁻ 當成設計值，門檻與增益看似留有大量餘裕；實際上落在 MPV 附近或更低的事件（斜入射把電荷分給相鄰像素、照射後電荷收集下降）會有一部分掉到門檻以下，命中效率從 99% 以上滑落，軌跡出現缺點，低動量軌跡的重建效率下降。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Designing on the 30,500 e⁻ mean makes threshold and gain look comfortably margined; in reality events near or below the MPV, such as inclined tracks sharing charge with neighbours or irradiated sensors collecting less, partly fall below threshold, hit efficiency slips from above 99%, tracks acquire missing hits and low-momentum reconstruction efficiency drops.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以 ⁹⁰Sr β 源（高能端電子近似 MIP）或測試束照射模組，先用讀出晶片內建的校正注入電容把 ToT 或 ADC 值換成電子數，再對叢集電荷擬合 Landau 與 Gauss 的摺積求 MPV 與寬度，與 22,000 e⁻ 的預期比較；同時在無照射時掃描門檻取得每個像素的 S 曲線，由其寬度求 ENC、由其中點求實際門檻分佈。","textEn":"Irradiate the module with a ⁹⁰Sr beta source, whose high-energy electrons approximate MIPs, or with a test beam; first convert ToT or ADC values into electrons with the readout chip's built-in calibration-injection capacitor, then fit a Landau convolved with a Gaussian to the cluster charge to obtain MPV and width and compare with the expected 22,000 e⁻. Without beam, scan the threshold to obtain each pixel's S-curve, taking ENC from its width and the true threshold distribution from its midpoints.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-03-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal\"?","options":["以 ⁹⁰Sr β 源（高能端電子近似 MIP）或測試束照射模組，先用讀出晶片內建的校正注入電容把 ToT 或 ADC 值換成電子數，再對叢集電荷擬合 Landau 與 Gauss 的摺積求 MPV 與寬度，與 22,000 e⁻ 的預期比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","感測器效率 99.9%，整個像素系統的效率就是 99.9%。"],"optionsEn":["Irradiate the module with a ⁹⁰Sr beta source, whose high-energy electrons approximate MIPs, or with a test beam.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If the sensor is 99.9% efficient, the whole pixel system is 99.9% efficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以 ⁹⁰Sr β 源（高能端電子近似 MIP）或測試束照射模組，先用讀出晶片內建的校正注入電容把 ToT 或 ADC 值換成電子數，再對叢集電荷擬合 Landau 與 Gauss 的摺積求 MPV 與寬度，與 22,000 e⁻ 的預期比較；同時在無照射時掃描門檻取得每個像素的 S 曲線，由其寬度求 ENC、由其中點求實際門檻分佈。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Irradiate the module with a ⁹⁰Sr beta source, whose high-energy electrons approximate MIPs, or with a test beam; first convert ToT or ADC values into electrons with the readout chip's built-in calibration-injection capacitor, then fit a Landau convolved with a Gaussian to the cluster charge to obtain MPV and width and compare with the expected 22,000 e⁻. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"a465-v12-04","title":"最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號：失效診斷","titleEn":"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「MIP 游離軌跡與訊號電荷」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “MIP ionisation track and signal charge” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"若把平均值 30,500 e⁻ 當成設計值，門檻與增益看似留有大量餘裕；實際上落在 MPV 附近或更低的事件（斜入射把電荷分給相鄰像素、照射後電荷收集下降）會有一部分掉到門檻以下，命中效率從 99% 以上滑落，軌跡出現缺點，低動量軌跡的重建效率下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Designing on the 30,500 e⁻ mean makes threshold and gain look comfortably margined; in reality events near or below the MPV, such as inclined tracks sharing charge with neighbours or irradiated sensors collecting less, partly fall below threshold, hit efficiency slips from above 99%, tracks acquire missing hits and low-momentum reconstruction efficiency drops. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：像素追蹤器的任務，就是在 LHC 25 ns 的束團間隔內把這數千到兩萬多個電子收集進讀出電路，並判斷它是否越過門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The pixel tracker's job is to collect these several thousand to twenty-odd thousand electrons into the readout circuit within the 25 ns LHC bunch spacing and decide whether they cross threshold.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每顆穿過像素的粒子都產生同樣多的電子，訊號是固定值。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every particle crossing a pixel frees the same number of electrons, so the signal is fixed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把平均值 30,500 e⁻ 當成設計值，門檻與增益看似留有大量餘裕；實際上落在 MPV 附近或更低的事件（斜入射把電荷分給相鄰像素、照射後電荷收集下降）會有一部分掉到門檻以下，命中效率從 99% 以上滑落，軌跡出現缺點，低動量軌跡的重建效率下降。","textEn":"Designing on the 30,500 e⁻ mean makes threshold and gain look comfortably margined; in reality events near or below the MPV, such as inclined tracks sharing charge with neighbours or irradiated sensors collecting less, partly fall below threshold, hit efficiency slips from above 99%, tracks acquire missing hits and low-momentum reconstruction efficiency drops.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「最小游離粒子能損與 Landau 訊號」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Minimum-ionising energy loss and the Landau signal\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","若把平均值 30,500 e⁻ 當成設計值，門檻與增益看似留有大量餘裕。","只要接上偏壓，整片感測器就全部是靈敏區，空乏深度與偏壓無關。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","Designing on the 30,500 e⁻ mean makes threshold and gain look comfortably margined.","Once bias is applied the whole sensor is sensitive, and depletion depth does not depend on voltage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若把平均值 30,500 e⁻ 當成設計值，門檻與增益看似留有大量餘裕；實際上落在 MPV 附近或更低的事件（斜入射把電荷分給相鄰像素、照射後電荷收集下降）會有一部分掉到門檻以下，命中效率從 99% 以上滑落，軌跡出現缺點，低動量軌跡的重建效率下降。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Designing on the 30,500 e⁻ mean makes threshold and gain look comfortably margined; in reality events near or below the MPV, such as inclined tracks sharing charge with neighbours or irradiated sensors collecting less, partly fall below threshold, hit efficiency slips from above 99%, tracks acquire missing hits and low-momentum reconstruction efficiency drops. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"a465-v12-05","title":"空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-04"],"objective":"說明「反向偏壓空乏區」如何決定矽像素粒子追蹤器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reverse-biased depletion region” determines the key performance of “Silicon-pixel particle trackers”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"矽感測器是一個大面積的反向偏壓 p–n 二極體，只有空乏區內產生的電荷會在電場中漂移並在讀出電極感應出訊號，未空乏區的電荷只能慢慢擴散甚至被複合，所以感測器必須全空乏或至少讓集電側空乏。空乏深度隨偏壓的平方根增加，全空乏電壓與有效摻雜濃度及厚度平方成正比。在 CMS 3.8 T 螺線管磁場中，漂移的電子受 Lorentz 力偏轉，使電荷橫向散到相鄰像素；工程上反而利用這個偏轉做電荷分享內插。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「反向偏壓空乏區」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A silicon sensor is a large-area reverse-biased p–n diode: only charge generated inside the depleted region drifts in the field and induces a signal on the readout electrode, whereas charge in undepleted silicon diffuses slowly or recombines, so the sensor must be fully depleted or at least depleted on the collecting side. Depletion depth grows with the square root of bias, and the full-depletion voltage scales with effective doping and the square of thickness. In the 3.8 T CMS solenoid field the drifting electrons are deflected by the Lorentz force and spread charge sideways into neighbouring pixels, an effect engineers exploit for charge-sharing interpolation. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Reverse-biased depletion region”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε).","failure":"常見誤解：「只要接上偏壓，整片感測器就全部是靈敏區，空乏深度與偏壓無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once bias is applied the whole sensor is sensitive, and depletion depth does not depend on voltage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「反向偏壓空乏區」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Reverse-biased depletion region”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-05-k1","title":"空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角","titleEn":"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle","text":"矽感測器是一個大面積的反向偏壓 p–n 二極體，只有空乏區內產生的電荷會在電場中漂移並在讀出電極感應出訊號，未空乏區的電荷只能慢慢擴散甚至被複合，所以感測器必須全空乏或至少讓集電側空乏。空乏深度隨偏壓的平方根增加，全空乏電壓與有效摻雜濃度及厚度平方成正比。","textEn":"A silicon sensor is a large-area reverse-biased p–n diode: only charge generated inside the depleted region drifts in the field and induces a signal on the readout electrode, whereas charge in undepleted silicon diffuses slowly or recombines, so the sensor must be fully depleted or at least depleted on the collecting side. Depletion depth grows with the square root of bias, and the full-depletion voltage scales with effective doping and the square of thickness.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要接上偏壓，整片感測器就全部是靈敏區，空乏深度與偏壓無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once bias is applied the whole sensor is sensitive, and depletion depth does not depend on voltage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle\" is correct?","options":["只要接上偏壓，整片感測器就全部是靈敏區，空乏深度與偏壓無關。","MAPS 只是把混合式像素做得更薄，輻射硬度與時間解析度完全相同。","矽感測器是一個大面積的反向偏壓 p–n 二極體，只有空乏區內產生的電荷會在電場中漂移並在讀出電極感應出訊號，未空乏區的電荷只能慢慢擴散甚至被複合，所以感測器必須全空乏或至少讓集電側空乏。"],"optionsEn":["Once bias is applied the whole sensor is sensitive, and depletion depth does not depend on voltage.","MAPS are simply thinner hybrid pixels with identical radiation hardness and timing.","A silicon sensor is a large-area reverse-biased p–n diode: only charge generated inside the depleted region drifts in the field and induces a signal on the readout electrode, whereas charge in undepleted silicon diffuses slowly or recombines, so the sensor must be fully depleted or at least depleted on the collecting side."],"answer":2,"explanation":"矽感測器是一個大面積的反向偏壓 p–n 二極體，只有空乏區內產生的電荷會在電場中漂移並在讀出電極感應出訊號，未空乏區的電荷只能慢慢擴散甚至被複合，所以感測器必須全空乏或至少讓集電側空乏。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A silicon sensor is a large-area reverse-biased p–n diode: only charge generated inside the depleted region drifts in the field and induces a signal on the readout electrode, whereas charge in undepleted silicon diffuses slowly or recombines, so the sensor must be fully depleted or at least depleted on the collecting side. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"a465-v12-06","title":"空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角：定量估算","titleEn":"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「反向偏壓空乏區」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reverse-biased depletion region” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε)。3 kΩ·cm n 型矽 N_eff = 1/(q·µ_e·ρ) ≈ 1.5×10¹² cm⁻³，d = 285 µm，ε = 11.9ε₀ = 1.05×10⁻¹² F/cm：V_d ≈ 1.6×10⁻¹⁹ × 1.54×10¹² × (0.0285 cm)²/(2 × 1.05×10⁻¹²) ≈ 95 V。偏壓 150 V（平均場 5.3 kV/cm）並考慮速度飽和，電子漂移約 6 ns、電洞約 14 ns。Lorentz 角 tanθ_L = r_H·µ·B ≈ 1.15 × 0.096 m²/(V·s) × 3.8 T ≈ 0.42，θ_L ≈ 23°，穿過 285 µm 的橫向偏移約 120 µm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε). For 3 kΩ·cm n-type silicon N_eff = 1/(q·µ_e·ρ) ≈ 1.5×10¹² cm⁻³; with d = 285 µm and ε = 11.9ε₀ = 1.05×10⁻¹² F/cm, V_d ≈ 1.6×10⁻¹⁹ × 1.54×10¹² × (0.0285 cm)²/(2 × 1.05×10⁻¹²) ≈ 95 V. At 150 V bias (mean field 5.3 kV/cm), including velocity saturation, electrons drift for about 6 ns and holes for about 14 ns. The Lorentz angle is tanθ_L = r_H·µ·B ≈ 1.15 × 0.096 m²/(V·s) × 3.8 T ≈ 0.42, θ_L ≈ 23°, a lateral shift of about 120 µm across 285 µm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：量 C–V 曲線：1/C² 對偏壓先線性上升，到全空乏處轉平，轉折點即 V_d；同時量 I–V 確認崩潰電壓遠高於工作點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure the C–V curve: 1/C² rises linearly with bias and flattens at full depletion, and the knee gives V_d; measure I–V at the same time to confirm that breakdown lies well above the operating point.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε)。3 kΩ·cm n 型矽 N_eff = 1/(q·µ_e·ρ) ≈ 1.5×10¹² cm⁻³，d = 285 µm，ε = 11.9ε₀ = 1.05×10⁻¹² F/cm：V_d ≈ 1.6×10⁻¹⁹ × 1.54×10¹² × (0.0285 cm)²/(2 × 1.05×10⁻¹²) ≈ 95 V。偏壓 150 V（平均場 5.3 kV/cm）並考慮速度飽和，電子漂移約 6 ns、電洞約 14 ns。Lorentz 角 tanθ_L = r_H·µ·B ≈ 1.15 × 0.096 m²/(V·s) × 3.8 T ≈ 0.42，θ_L ≈ 23°，穿過 285 µm 的橫向偏移約 120 µm。","textEn":"V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε). For 3 kΩ·cm n-type silicon N_eff = 1/(q·µ_e·ρ) ≈ 1.5×10¹² cm⁻³; with d = 285 µm and ε = 11.9ε₀ = 1.05×10⁻¹² F/cm, V_d ≈ 1.6×10⁻¹⁹ × 1.54×10¹² × (0.0285 cm)²/(2 × 1.05×10⁻¹²) ≈ 95 V. At 150 V bias (mean field 5.3 kV/cm), including velocity saturation, electrons drift for about 6 ns and holes for about 14 ns. The Lorentz angle is tanθ_L = r_H·µ·B ≈ 1.15 × 0.096 m²/(V·s) × 3.8 T ≈ 0.42, θ_L ≈ 23°, a lateral shift of about 120 µm across 285 µm.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle\", which statement holds?","options":["V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε)。","解析度就等於像素節距，100 µm 節距不可能量到 10 µm 的位置。","感測器效率 99.9%，整個像素系統的效率就是 99.9%。"],"optionsEn":["V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε).","Resolution equals the pixel pitch, so a 100 µm pitch cannot measure position to 10 µm.","If the sensor is 99.9% efficient, the whole pixel system is 99.9% efficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"V_d = q·N_eff·d²/(2ε). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"a465-v12-07","title":"空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「反向偏壓空乏區」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Reverse-biased depletion region” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"量 C–V 曲線：1/C² 對偏壓先線性上升，到全空乏處轉平，轉折點即 V_d；同時量 I–V 確認崩潰電壓遠高於工作點。Lorentz 角在磁場中以入射角掃描量測：叢集寬度對入射角的曲線最小值所在的角度就是 Lorentz 角，與 r_H·µ·B 的預測比較，並在每次改變偏壓後重做。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure the C–V curve: 1/C² rises linearly with bias and flattens at full depletion, and the knee gives V_d; measure I–V at the same time to confirm that breakdown lies well above the operating point. Measure the Lorentz angle in field by scanning the incidence angle: the angle at which cluster width versus incidence reaches its minimum is the Lorentz angle, which is compared with the r_H·µ·B prediction and re-measured whenever the bias changes. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：偏壓不足時集電側以外留有未空乏層，電荷收集變慢且部分被複合，訊號下降並出現落在下一個 25 ns 時窗的晚到命中；若重建沿用錯誤的 Lorentz 偏移，所有命中位置系統性偏移數十 µm，在桶部兩個方向相反的模組上產生方向相反的殘差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: With insufficient bias an undepleted layer remains beyond the collecting side, charge collection slows and partly recombines, the signal drops and late hits spill into the next 25 ns window; if reconstruction keeps a wrong Lorentz shift, every hit is displaced by tens of micrometres, producing opposite residuals on barrel modules mounted in opposite orientations.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量 C–V 曲線：1/C² 對偏壓先線性上升，到全空乏處轉平，轉折點即 V_d；同時量 I–V 確認崩潰電壓遠高於工作點。Lorentz 角在磁場中以入射角掃描量測：叢集寬度對入射角的曲線最小值所在的角度就是 Lorentz 角，與 r_H·µ·B 的預測比較，並在每次改變偏壓後重做。","textEn":"Measure the C–V curve: 1/C² rises linearly with bias and flattens at full depletion, and the knee gives V_d; measure I–V at the same time to confirm that breakdown lies well above the operating point. Measure the Lorentz angle in field by scanning the incidence angle: the angle at which cluster width versus incidence reaches its minimum is the Lorentz angle, which is compared with the r_H·µ·B prediction and re-measured whenever the bias changes.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-07-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","量 C–V 曲線：1/C² 對偏壓先線性上升，到全空乏處轉平，轉折點即 V_d；同時量 I–V 確認崩潰電壓遠高於工作點。","殘差分佈置中且很窄，就代表追蹤器幾何已完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Measure the C–V curve: 1/C² rises linearly with bias and flattens at full depletion, and the knee gives V_d.","Centred, narrow residual distributions prove the tracker geometry is completely correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"量 C–V 曲線：1/C² 對偏壓先線性上升，到全空乏處轉平，轉折點即 V_d；同時量 I–V 確認崩潰電壓遠高於工作點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure the C–V curve: 1/C² rises linearly with bias and flattens at full depletion, and the knee gives V_d; measure I–V at the same time to confirm that breakdown lies well above the operating point. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"a465-v12-08","title":"空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角：失效診斷","titleEn":"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「反向偏壓空乏區」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Reverse-biased depletion region” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"偏壓不足時集電側以外留有未空乏層，電荷收集變慢且部分被複合，訊號下降並出現落在下一個 25 ns 時窗的晚到命中；若重建沿用錯誤的 Lorentz 偏移，所有命中位置系統性偏移數十 µm，在桶部兩個方向相反的模組上產生方向相反的殘差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"With insufficient bias an undepleted layer remains beyond the collecting side, charge collection slows and partly recombines, the signal drops and late hits spill into the next 25 ns window; if reconstruction keeps a wrong Lorentz shift, every hit is displaced by tens of micrometres, producing opposite residuals on barrel modules mounted in opposite orientations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：在 CMS 3.8 T 螺線管磁場中，漂移的電子受 Lorentz 力偏轉，使電荷橫向散到相鄰像素；工程上反而利用這個偏轉做電荷分享內插。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In the 3.8 T CMS solenoid field the drifting electrons are deflected by the Lorentz force and spread charge sideways into neighbouring pixels, an effect engineers exploit for charge-sharing interpolation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要接上偏壓，整片感測器就全部是靈敏區，空乏深度與偏壓無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once bias is applied the whole sensor is sensitive, and depletion depth does not depend on voltage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"偏壓不足時集電側以外留有未空乏層，電荷收集變慢且部分被複合，訊號下降並出現落在下一個 25 ns 時窗的晚到命中；若重建沿用錯誤的 Lorentz 偏移，所有命中位置系統性偏移數十 µm，在桶部兩個方向相反的模組上產生方向相反的殘差。","textEn":"With insufficient bias an undepleted layer remains beyond the collecting side, charge collection slows and partly recombines, the signal drops and late hits spill into the next 25 ns window; if reconstruction keeps a wrong Lorentz shift, every hit is displaced by tens of micrometres, producing opposite residuals on barrel modules mounted in opposite orientations.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空乏電壓、漂移時間與 Lorentz 角」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Depletion voltage, drift time and the Lorentz angle\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","MAPS 只是把混合式像素做得更薄，輻射硬度與時間解析度完全相同。","偏壓不足時集電側以外留有未空乏層，電荷收集變慢且部分被複合，訊號下降並出現落在下一個 25 ns 時窗的晚到命中。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","MAPS are simply thinner hybrid pixels with identical radiation hardness and timing.","With insufficient bias an undepleted layer remains beyond the collecting side, charge collection slows and partly recombines, the signal drops and late hits spill into the next 25 ns window."],"answer":2,"explanation":"偏壓不足時集電側以外留有未空乏層，電荷收集變慢且部分被複合，訊號下降並出現落在下一個 25 ns 時窗的晚到命中；若重建沿用錯誤的 Lorentz 偏移，所有命中位置系統性偏移數十 µm，在桶部兩個方向相反的模組上產生方向相反的殘差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"With insufficient bias an undepleted layer remains beyond the collecting side, charge collection slows and partly recombines, the signal drops and late hits spill into the next 25 ns window; if reconstruction keeps a wrong Lorentz shift, every hit is displaced by tens of micrometres, producing opposite residuals on barrel modules mounted in opposite orientations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"a465-v12-s2","title":"元件、材料與製造","titleEn":"Components, materials and fabrication","description":"本階段聚焦「混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構」與「輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS\" and \"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a465-v12-09","title":"混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-08"],"objective":"說明「感測器、凸塊與讀出晶片」如何決定矽像素粒子追蹤器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sensor, bump bonds and readout chip” determines the key performance of “Silicon-pixel particle trackers”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"混合式像素把高阻值感測器與 CMOS 讀出晶片分開製造，再以每像素一顆的焊錫或銦凸塊倒裝接合，因此感測器可採 n-in-n 或 n-in-p 的抗輻射設計，讀出晶片可用先進製程；CMS Phase-1 像素為 100×150 µm²、285 µm 厚，每顆讀出晶片 52×80 像素。單體式主動像素感測器（MAPS）把電荷收集層與前端電路做在同一片晶圓上，例如 ALICE ITS2 的 ALPIDE 以 180 nm CMOS 影像感測製程製作約 29×27 µm² 的像素並薄化到 50 µm，省去凸塊與第二層矽；代價是電荷主要來自數十微米的磊晶層，抗輻射能力與時間解析度不如混合式。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「感測器、凸塊與讀出晶片」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hybrid pixels fabricate a high-resistivity sensor and a CMOS readout chip separately and flip-chip join them with one solder or indium bump per pixel, so the sensor can use radiation-hard n-in-n or n-in-p designs while the readout chip uses an advanced process; CMS Phase-1 pixels are 100×150 µm², 285 µm thick, with 52×80 pixels per readout chip. Monolithic active pixel sensors (MAPS) put the charge-collecting layer and front-end circuit in the same wafer; ALICE ITS2's ALPIDE uses a 180 nm CMOS imaging process with pixels of about 29×27 µm² thinned to 50 µm, eliminating bumps and a second silicon layer, at the cost of collecting charge mainly from an epitaxial layer tens of micrometres thick and having lower radiation tolerance and timing performance than hybrids. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Sensor, bump bonds and readout chip”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：面積比 (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19；二元解析度 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm 對 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Area ratio (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19; binary resolution 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm versus 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm.","failure":"常見誤解：「MAPS 只是把混合式像素做得更薄，輻射硬度與時間解析度完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"MAPS are simply thinner hybrid pixels with identical radiation hardness and timing.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「感測器、凸塊與讀出晶片」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Sensor, bump bonds and readout chip”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-09-k1","title":"混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構","titleEn":"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS","text":"混合式像素把高阻值感測器與 CMOS 讀出晶片分開製造，再以每像素一顆的焊錫或銦凸塊倒裝接合，因此感測器可採 n-in-n 或 n-in-p 的抗輻射設計，讀出晶片可用先進製程；CMS Phase-1 像素為 100×150 µm²、285 µm 厚，每顆讀出晶片 52×80 像素。單體式主動像素感測器（MAPS）把電荷收集層與前端電路做在同一片晶圓上，例如 ALICE ITS2 的 ALPIDE 以 180 nm CMOS 影像感測製程製作約 29×27 µm² 的像素並薄化到 50 µm，省去凸塊與第二層矽；代價是電荷主要來自數十微米的磊晶層，抗輻射能力與時間解析度不如混合式。","textEn":"Hybrid pixels fabricate a high-resistivity sensor and a CMOS readout chip separately and flip-chip join them with one solder or indium bump per pixel, so the sensor can use radiation-hard n-in-n or n-in-p designs while the readout chip uses an advanced process; CMS Phase-1 pixels are 100×150 µm², 285 µm thick, with 52×80 pixels per readout chip. Monolithic active pixel sensors (MAPS) put the charge-collecting layer and front-end circuit in the same wafer; ALICE ITS2's ALPIDE uses a 180 nm CMOS imaging process with pixels of about 29×27 µm² thinned to 50 µm, eliminating bumps and a second silicon layer, at the cost of collecting charge mainly from an epitaxial layer tens of micrometres thick and having lower radiation tolerance and timing performance than hybrids.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：MAPS 只是把混合式像素做得更薄，輻射硬度與時間解析度完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: MAPS are simply thinner hybrid pixels with identical radiation hardness and timing. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS\" is correct?","options":["混合式像素把高阻值感測器與 CMOS 讀出晶片分開製造，再以每像素一顆的焊錫或銦凸塊倒裝接合，因此感測器可採 n-in-n 或 n-in-p 的抗輻射設計，讀出晶片可用先進製程。","MAPS 只是把混合式像素做得更薄，輻射硬度與時間解析度完全相同。","漏電流只取決於累積的輻射劑量，與運轉溫度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Hybrid pixels fabricate a high-resistivity sensor and a CMOS readout chip separately and flip-chip join them with one solder or indium bump per pixel, so the sensor can use radiation-hard n-in-n or n-in-p designs while the readout chip uses an advanced process.","MAPS are simply thinner hybrid pixels with identical radiation hardness and timing.","Leakage current depends only on accumulated radiation dose, not on operating temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"混合式像素把高阻值感測器與 CMOS 讀出晶片分開製造，再以每像素一顆的焊錫或銦凸塊倒裝接合，因此感測器可採 n-in-n 或 n-in-p 的抗輻射設計，讀出晶片可用先進製程；CMS Phase-1 像素為 100×150 µm²、285 µm 厚，每顆讀出晶片 52×80 像素。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hybrid pixels fabricate a high-resistivity sensor and a CMOS readout chip separately and flip-chip join them with one solder or indium bump per pixel, so the sensor can use radiation-hard n-in-n or n-in-p designs while the readout chip uses an advanced process; CMS Phase-1 pixels are 100×150 µm², 285 µm thick, with 52×80 pixels per readout chip. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"a465-v12-10","title":"混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構：定量估算","titleEn":"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「感測器、凸塊與讀出晶片」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sensor, bump bonds and readout chip” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：面積比 (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19；二元解析度 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm 對 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm。物質量（矽 X₀ = 9.37 cm）：285 µm 感測器 ≈ 0.30% X₀，175 µm 讀出晶片 ≈ 0.19% X₀；50 µm MAPS 僅 ≈ 0.053% X₀。MAPS 收集電極電容約 5 fF，1,300 e⁻ 產生 ΔV = Q/C ≈ 42 mV，可用極低功耗的像素內放大器判斷；混合式輸入電容約 150 fF，需要電荷靈敏放大器。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Area ratio (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19; binary resolution 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm versus 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm. Material (silicon X₀ = 9.37 cm): a 285 µm sensor is ≈ 0.30% X₀ and a 175 µm readout chip ≈ 0.19% X₀, whereas a 50 µm MAPS is only ≈ 0.053% X₀. A MAPS collection electrode of about 5 fF turns 1,300 e⁻ into ΔV = Q/C ≈ 42 mV, enough for a very low-power in-pixel amplifier; a hybrid input of about 150 fF needs a charge-sensitive amplifier. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：混合式模組以放射源或 X 光全面照射建立凸塊連通圖，並比較偏壓開與關時每個像素的雜訊差，找出斷開或短路的凸塊；MAPS 在測試束量效率與假命中率對門檻的曲線，確認在效率高於 99% 的門檻下，假命中率低於每像素每事件 10⁻⁶。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: For hybrid modules, illuminate the whole module with a source or X-rays to map bump connectivity and compare each pixel's noise with bias on and off to locate open or shorted bumps; for MAPS, measure efficiency and fake-hit rate versus threshold in a test beam and confirm that at a threshold giving above 99% efficiency the fake-hit rate stays below 10⁻⁶ per pixel per event.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"面積比 (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19；二元解析度 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm 對 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm。物質量（矽 X₀ = 9.37 cm）：285 µm 感測器 ≈ 0.30% X₀，175 µm 讀出晶片 ≈ 0.19% X₀；50 µm MAPS 僅 ≈ 0.053% X₀。MAPS 收集電極電容約 5 fF，1,300 e⁻ 產生 ΔV = Q/C ≈ 42 mV，可用極低功耗的像素內放大器判斷；混合式輸入電容約 150 fF，需要電荷靈敏放大器。","textEn":"Area ratio (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19; binary resolution 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm versus 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm. Material (silicon X₀ = 9.37 cm): a 285 µm sensor is ≈ 0.30% X₀ and a 175 µm readout chip ≈ 0.19% X₀, whereas a 50 µm MAPS is only ≈ 0.053% X₀. A MAPS collection electrode of about 5 fF turns 1,300 e⁻ into ΔV = Q/C ≈ 42 mV, enough for a very low-power in-pixel amplifier; a hybrid input of about 150 fF needs a charge-sensitive amplifier.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS\", which statement holds?","options":["像素越小，頂點解析度一定越好，與物質量無關。","面積比 (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19；二元解析度 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm 對 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm。","殘差分佈置中且很窄，就代表追蹤器幾何已完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Smaller pixels always give better vertex resolution regardless of material.","Area ratio (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19; binary resolution 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm versus 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm.","Centred, narrow residual distributions prove the tracker geometry is completely correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"面積比 (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19；二元解析度 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm 對 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Area ratio (100×150)/(29.24×26.88) ≈ 19; binary resolution 100/√12 ≈ 28.9 µm versus 29.24/√12 ≈ 8.4 µm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"a465-v12-11","title":"混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「感測器、凸塊與讀出晶片」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Sensor, bump bonds and readout chip” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"混合式模組以放射源或 X 光全面照射建立凸塊連通圖，並比較偏壓開與關時每個像素的雜訊差，找出斷開或短路的凸塊；MAPS 在測試束量效率與假命中率對門檻的曲線，確認在效率高於 99% 的門檻下，假命中率低於每像素每事件 10⁻⁶。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"For hybrid modules, illuminate the whole module with a source or X-rays to map bump connectivity and compare each pixel's noise with bias on and off to locate open or shorted bumps; for MAPS, measure efficiency and fake-hit rate versus threshold in a test beam and confirm that at a threshold giving above 99% efficiency the fake-hit rate stays below 10⁻⁶ per pixel per event. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：凸塊在熱循環中因感測器與讀出晶片的熱應變差而開裂，該像素變成死像素，雜訊反而下降，若只用雜訊判斷健康就會漏抓；MAPS 若磊晶層太薄或反向偏壓不足，電荷擴散到多個像素後各自低於門檻，效率下降且叢集形狀異常。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Bumps crack under thermal cycling because of differential strain between sensor and readout chip, turning the pixel dead while its noise actually falls, so a noise-only health check misses it; in MAPS a thin epitaxial layer or insufficient reverse bias lets charge diffuse over several pixels that each stay below threshold, lowering efficiency and distorting cluster shapes.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"混合式模組以放射源或 X 光全面照射建立凸塊連通圖，並比較偏壓開與關時每個像素的雜訊差，找出斷開或短路的凸塊；MAPS 在測試束量效率與假命中率對門檻的曲線，確認在效率高於 99% 的門檻下，假命中率低於每像素每事件 10⁻⁶。","textEn":"For hybrid modules, illuminate the whole module with a source or X-rays to map bump connectivity and compare each pixel's noise with bias on and off to locate open or shorted bumps; for MAPS, measure efficiency and fake-hit rate versus threshold in a test beam and confirm that at a threshold giving above 99% efficiency the fake-hit rate stays below 10⁻⁶ per pixel per event.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-11-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS\"?","options":["只看單次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準件或重複量測。","每顆穿過像素的粒子都產生同樣多的電子，訊號是固定值。","混合式模組以放射源或 X 光全面照射建立凸塊連通圖，並比較偏壓開與關時每個像素的雜訊差，找出斷開或短路的凸塊。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the result; no reference artefact or repeat measurement is needed.","Every particle crossing a pixel frees the same number of electrons, so the signal is fixed.","For hybrid modules, illuminate the whole module with a source or X-rays to map bump connectivity and compare each pixel's noise with bias on and off to locate open or shorted bumps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"混合式模組以放射源或 X 光全面照射建立凸塊連通圖，並比較偏壓開與關時每個像素的雜訊差，找出斷開或短路的凸塊；MAPS 在測試束量效率與假命中率對門檻的曲線，確認在效率高於 99% 的門檻下，假命中率低於每像素每事件 10⁻⁶。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"For hybrid modules, illuminate the whole module with a source or X-rays to map bump connectivity and compare each pixel's noise with bias on and off to locate open or shorted bumps; for MAPS, measure efficiency and fake-hit rate versus threshold in a test beam and confirm that at a threshold giving above 99% efficiency the fake-hit rate stays below 10⁻⁶ per pixel per event. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"a465-v12-12","title":"混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「感測器、凸塊與讀出晶片」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Sensor, bump bonds and readout chip” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"凸塊在熱循環中因感測器與讀出晶片的熱應變差而開裂，該像素變成死像素，雜訊反而下降，若只用雜訊判斷健康就會漏抓；MAPS 若磊晶層太薄或反向偏壓不足，電荷擴散到多個像素後各自低於門檻，效率下降且叢集形狀異常。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Bumps crack under thermal cycling because of differential strain between sensor and readout chip, turning the pixel dead while its noise actually falls, so a noise-only health check misses it; in MAPS a thin epitaxial layer or insufficient reverse bias lets charge diffuse over several pixels that each stay below threshold, lowering efficiency and distorting cluster shapes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：單體式主動像素感測器（MAPS）把電荷收集層與前端電路做在同一片晶圓上，例如 ALICE ITS2 的 ALPIDE 以 180 nm CMOS 影像感測製程製作約 29×27 µm² 的像素並薄化到 50 µm，省去凸塊與第二層矽；代價是電荷主要來自數十微米的磊晶層，抗輻射能力與時間解析度不如混合式。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Monolithic active pixel sensors (MAPS) put the charge-collecting layer and front-end circuit in the same wafer; ALICE ITS2's ALPIDE uses a 180 nm CMOS imaging process with pixels of about 29×27 µm² thinned to 50 µm, eliminating bumps and a second silicon layer, at the cost of collecting charge mainly from an epitaxial layer tens of micrometres thick and having lower radiation tolerance and timing performance than hybrids.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「MAPS 只是把混合式像素做得更薄，輻射硬度與時間解析度完全相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"MAPS are simply thinner hybrid pixels with identical radiation hardness and timing.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"凸塊在熱循環中因感測器與讀出晶片的熱應變差而開裂，該像素變成死像素，雜訊反而下降，若只用雜訊判斷健康就會漏抓；MAPS 若磊晶層太薄或反向偏壓不足，電荷擴散到多個像素後各自低於門檻，效率下降且叢集形狀異常。","textEn":"Bumps crack under thermal cycling because of differential strain between sensor and readout chip, turning the pixel dead while its noise actually falls, so a noise-only health check misses it; in MAPS a thin epitaxial layer or insufficient reverse bias lets charge diffuse over several pixels that each stay below threshold, lowering efficiency and distorting cluster shapes.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「混合式像素與單體式 MAPS 架構」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hybrid pixels versus monolithic MAPS\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["凸塊在熱循環中因感測器與讀出晶片的熱應變差而開裂，該像素變成死像素，雜訊反而下降，若只用雜訊判斷健康就會漏抓。","異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","漏電流只取決於累積的輻射劑量，與運轉溫度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Bumps crack under thermal cycling because of differential strain between sensor and readout chip, turning the pixel dead while its noise actually falls, so a noise-only health check misses it.","An anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Leakage current depends only on accumulated radiation dose, not on operating temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"凸塊在熱循環中因感測器與讀出晶片的熱應變差而開裂，該像素變成死像素，雜訊反而下降，若只用雜訊判斷健康就會漏抓；MAPS 若磊晶層太薄或反向偏壓不足，電荷擴散到多個像素後各自低於門檻，效率下降且叢集形狀異常。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Bumps crack under thermal cycling because of differential strain between sensor and readout chip, turning the pixel dead while its noise actually falls, so a noise-only health check misses it; in MAPS a thin epitaxial layer or insufficient reverse bias lets charge diffuse over several pixels that each stay below threshold, lowering efficiency and distorting cluster shapes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"a465-v12-13","title":"輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-12"],"objective":"說明「感測器漏電流與冷卻迴路」如何決定矽像素粒子追蹤器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sensor leakage current and cooling loop” determines the key performance of “Silicon-pixel particle trackers”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"強子與高能粒子在矽晶格中造成位移損傷，以 1 MeV 中子等效通量 Φ_eq 計量，產生能隙中間的缺陷能階，帶來三種後果：漏電流依 ΔI = α·Φ_eq·V 線性增加；有效摻雜改變，使 n 型基體發生型別反轉並讓空乏電壓持續上升；以及載子被缺陷捕獲使收集電荷下降。漏電流依 T²·exp(−E_eff/(2k_B·T)) 強烈依賴溫度，約每降 7 K 減半，所以內層像素必須冷到攝氏零下十到二十度；漏電流發熱又會加熱感測器，冷卻不足就會形成熱失控。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「感測器漏電流與冷卻迴路」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hadrons and energetic particles cause displacement damage in the silicon lattice, quantified by the 1 MeV neutron-equivalent fluence Φ_eq, creating mid-gap defect levels with three consequences: leakage current rises linearly as ΔI = α·Φ_eq·V; effective doping changes, inverting n-type bulk and steadily raising the depletion voltage; and carriers are trapped, reducing collected charge. Leakage follows T²·exp(−E_eff/(2k_B·T)) and roughly halves for every 7 K of cooling, so inner pixel layers must run at −10 to −20 °C; because the leakage current itself heats the sensor, insufficient cooling leads to thermal runaway. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Sensor leakage current and cooling loop”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm（20 °C、退火後）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm at 20 °C after annealing.","failure":"常見誤解：「漏電流只取決於累積的輻射劑量，與運轉溫度無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Leakage current depends only on accumulated radiation dose, not on operating temperature.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「感測器漏電流與冷卻迴路」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Sensor leakage current and cooling loop”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-13-k1","title":"輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控","titleEn":"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway","text":"強子與高能粒子在矽晶格中造成位移損傷，以 1 MeV 中子等效通量 Φ_eq 計量，產生能隙中間的缺陷能階，帶來三種後果：漏電流依 ΔI = α·Φ_eq·V 線性增加；有效摻雜改變，使 n 型基體發生型別反轉並讓空乏電壓持續上升；以及載子被缺陷捕獲使收集電荷下降。漏電流依 T²·exp(−E_eff/(2k_B·T)) 強烈依賴溫度，約每降 7 K 減半，所以內層像素必須冷到攝氏零下十到二十度；漏電流發熱又會加熱感測器，冷卻不足就會形成熱失控。","textEn":"Hadrons and energetic particles cause displacement damage in the silicon lattice, quantified by the 1 MeV neutron-equivalent fluence Φ_eq, creating mid-gap defect levels with three consequences: leakage current rises linearly as ΔI = α·Φ_eq·V; effective doping changes, inverting n-type bulk and steadily raising the depletion voltage; and carriers are trapped, reducing collected charge. Leakage follows T²·exp(−E_eff/(2k_B·T)) and roughly halves for every 7 K of cooling, so inner pixel layers must run at −10 to −20 °C; because the leakage current itself heats the sensor, insufficient cooling leads to thermal runaway.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：漏電流只取決於累積的輻射劑量，與運轉溫度無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Leakage current depends only on accumulated radiation dose, not on operating temperature. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway\" is correct?","options":["漏電流只取決於累積的輻射劑量，與運轉溫度無關。","強子與高能粒子在矽晶格中造成位移損傷，以 1 MeV 中子等效通量 Φ_eq 計量，產生能隙中間的缺陷能階，帶來三種後果：漏電流依 ΔI = α·Φ_eq·V 線性增加。","解析度就等於像素節距，100 µm 節距不可能量到 10 µm 的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Leakage current depends only on accumulated radiation dose, not on operating temperature.","Hadrons and energetic particles cause displacement damage in the silicon lattice, quantified by the 1 MeV neutron-equivalent fluence Φ_eq, creating mid-gap defect levels with three consequences: leakage current rises linearly as ΔI = α·Φ_eq·V.","Resolution equals the pixel pitch, so a 100 µm pitch cannot measure position to 10 µm."],"answer":1,"explanation":"強子與高能粒子在矽晶格中造成位移損傷，以 1 MeV 中子等效通量 Φ_eq 計量，產生能隙中間的缺陷能階，帶來三種後果：漏電流依 ΔI = α·Φ_eq·V 線性增加；有效摻雜改變，使 n 型基體發生型別反轉並讓空乏電壓持續上升；以及載子被缺陷捕獲使收集電荷下降。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hadrons and energetic particles cause displacement damage in the silicon lattice, quantified by the 1 MeV neutron-equivalent fluence Φ_eq, creating mid-gap defect levels with three consequences: leakage current rises linearly as ΔI = α·Φ_eq·V; effective doping changes, inverting n-type bulk and steadily raising the depletion voltage; and carriers are trapped, reducing collected charge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"a465-v12-14","title":"輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控：定量估算","titleEn":"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「感測器漏電流與冷卻迴路」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sensor leakage current and cooling loop” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm（20 °C、退火後）。100×150×285 µm³ 像素體積 4.28×10⁻⁶ cm³，Φ_eq = 1×10¹⁵ cm⁻² 時 20 °C 漏電流 ≈ 171 nA；換到 −10 °C 乘以 (263/293)²·exp[−1.21 eV/(2k_B)·(1/263 − 1/293)] ≈ 0.053，約 9 nA。66,560 像素的模組約 0.6 mA，400 V 偏壓下發熱 0.24 W。型別反轉後 N_eff ≈ g_c·Φ ≈ 1.5×10¹³ cm⁻³，285 µm 的空乏電壓升到約 930 V，超過偏壓上限，只能部分空乏運作。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm at 20 °C after annealing. A 100×150×285 µm³ pixel has a volume of 4.28×10⁻⁶ cm³, so at Φ_eq = 1×10¹⁵ cm⁻² it leaks about 171 nA at 20 °C; scaling to −10 °C multiplies by (263/293)²·exp[−1.21 eV/(2k_B)·(1/263 − 1/293)] ≈ 0.053, about 9 nA. A 66,560-pixel module then draws about 0.6 mA and dissipates 0.24 W at 400 V. After inversion N_eff ≈ g_c·Φ ≈ 1.5×10¹³ cm⁻³ and the 285 µm depletion voltage climbs to about 930 V, beyond the bias limit, so the sensor runs partially depleted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：運轉期間定期量 I–V，把電流換算到 20 °C 再除以感測器體積，畫漏電流對累積亮度或模擬通量的直線，斜率應與 α 相符；以偏壓掃描量叢集電荷對偏壓的曲線求有效空乏電壓，決定何時提高偏壓；再比對各模組溫度感測值與漏電流的溫度相依性，找出熱接觸不良的模組。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: During operation take periodic I–V scans, normalise the current to 20 °C and divide by sensor volume, and plot leakage against integrated luminosity or simulated fluence, expecting a slope consistent with α; use bias scans of cluster charge versus voltage to find the effective depletion voltage and decide when to raise bias; compare each module's temperature readings with the temperature dependence of its leakage to identify modules with poor thermal contact.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm（20 °C、退火後）。100×150×285 µm³ 像素體積 4.28×10⁻⁶ cm³，Φ_eq = 1×10¹⁵ cm⁻² 時 20 °C 漏電流 ≈ 171 nA；換到 −10 °C 乘以 (263/293)²·exp[−1.21 eV/(2k_B)·(1/263 − 1/293)] ≈ 0.053，約 9 nA。66,560 像素的模組約 0.6 mA，400 V 偏壓下發熱 0.24 W。型別反轉後 N_eff ≈ g_c·Φ ≈ 1.5×10¹³ cm⁻³，285 µm 的空乏電壓升到約 930 V，超過偏壓上限，只能部分空乏運作。","textEn":"α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm at 20 °C after annealing. A 100×150×285 µm³ pixel has a volume of 4.28×10⁻⁶ cm³, so at Φ_eq = 1×10¹⁵ cm⁻² it leaks about 171 nA at 20 °C; scaling to −10 °C multiplies by (263/293)²·exp[−1.21 eV/(2k_B)·(1/263 − 1/293)] ≈ 0.053, about 9 nA. A 66,560-pixel module then draws about 0.6 mA and dissipates 0.24 W at 400 V. After inversion N_eff ≈ g_c·Φ ≈ 1.5×10¹³ cm⁻³ and the 285 µm depletion voltage climbs to about 930 V, beyond the bias limit, so the sensor runs partially depleted.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway\", which statement holds?","options":["感測器效率 99.9%，整個像素系統的效率就是 99.9%。","每顆穿過像素的粒子都產生同樣多的電子，訊號是固定值。","α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm（20 °C、退火後）。"],"optionsEn":["If the sensor is 99.9% efficient, the whole pixel system is 99.9% efficient.","Every particle crossing a pixel frees the same number of electrons, so the signal is fixed.","α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm at 20 °C after annealing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm（20 °C、退火後）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"α ≈ 4×10⁻¹⁷ A/cm at 20 °C after annealing. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"a465-v12-15","title":"輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「感測器漏電流與冷卻迴路」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Sensor leakage current and cooling loop” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"運轉期間定期量 I–V，把電流換算到 20 °C 再除以感測器體積，畫漏電流對累積亮度或模擬通量的直線，斜率應與 α 相符；以偏壓掃描量叢集電荷對偏壓的曲線求有效空乏電壓，決定何時提高偏壓；再比對各模組溫度感測值與漏電流的溫度相依性，找出熱接觸不良的模組。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"During operation take periodic I–V scans, normalise the current to 20 °C and divide by sensor volume, and plot leakage against integrated luminosity or simulated fluence, expecting a slope consistent with α; use bias scans of cluster charge versus voltage to find the effective depletion voltage and decide when to raise bias; compare each module's temperature readings with the temperature dependence of its leakage to identify modules with poor thermal contact. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：冷卻板與模組間的導熱膠脫層時，局部溫度升高約 7 K 就讓漏電流加倍，發熱再推高溫度，最終電源電流達上限而跳脫，該模組退出運轉；若偏壓未隨空乏電壓上升而調高，收集電荷持續下降，效率先在最內層崩落。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: When the thermal adhesive between cooling plate and module delaminates, a local rise of about 7 K doubles the leakage, the extra heat raises temperature further, and the supply eventually hits its current limit and trips, removing the module; if bias is not raised as the depletion voltage climbs, collected charge keeps falling and efficiency collapses first in the innermost layer.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"運轉期間定期量 I–V，把電流換算到 20 °C 再除以感測器體積，畫漏電流對累積亮度或模擬通量的直線，斜率應與 α 相符；以偏壓掃描量叢集電荷對偏壓的曲線求有效空乏電壓，決定何時提高偏壓；再比對各模組溫度感測值與漏電流的溫度相依性，找出熱接觸不良的模組。","textEn":"During operation take periodic I–V scans, normalise the current to 20 °C and divide by sensor volume, and plot leakage against integrated luminosity or simulated fluence, expecting a slope consistent with α; use bias scans of cluster charge versus voltage to find the effective depletion voltage and decide when to raise bias; compare each module's temperature readings with the temperature dependence of its leakage to identify modules with poor thermal contact.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-15-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway\"?","options":["運轉期間定期量 I–V，把電流換算到 20 °C 再除以感測器體積，畫漏電流對累積亮度或模擬通量的直線，斜率應與 α 相符。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要接上偏壓，整片感測器就全部是靈敏區，空乏深度與偏壓無關。"],"optionsEn":["During operation take periodic I–V scans, normalise the current to 20 °C and divide by sensor volume, and plot leakage against integrated luminosity or simulated fluence, expecting a slope consistent with α.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Once bias is applied the whole sensor is sensitive, and depletion depth does not depend on voltage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"運轉期間定期量 I–V，把電流換算到 20 °C 再除以感測器體積，畫漏電流對累積亮度或模擬通量的直線，斜率應與 α 相符；以偏壓掃描量叢集電荷對偏壓的曲線求有效空乏電壓，決定何時提高偏壓；再比對各模組溫度感測值與漏電流的溫度相依性，找出熱接觸不良的模組。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"During operation take periodic I–V scans, normalise the current to 20 °C and divide by sensor volume, and plot leakage against integrated luminosity or simulated fluence, expecting a slope consistent with α; use bias scans of cluster charge versus voltage to find the effective depletion voltage and decide when to raise bias; compare each module's temperature readings with the temperature dependence of its leakage to identify modules with poor thermal contact. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"a465-v12-16","title":"輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控：失效診斷","titleEn":"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「感測器漏電流與冷卻迴路」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Sensor leakage current and cooling loop” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"冷卻板與模組間的導熱膠脫層時，局部溫度升高約 7 K 就讓漏電流加倍，發熱再推高溫度，最終電源電流達上限而跳脫，該模組退出運轉；若偏壓未隨空乏電壓上升而調高，收集電荷持續下降，效率先在最內層崩落。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"When the thermal adhesive between cooling plate and module delaminates, a local rise of about 7 K doubles the leakage, the extra heat raises temperature further, and the supply eventually hits its current limit and trips, removing the module; if bias is not raised as the depletion voltage climbs, collected charge keeps falling and efficiency collapses first in the innermost layer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：漏電流依 T²·exp(−E_eff/(2k_B·T)) 強烈依賴溫度，約每降 7 K 減半，所以內層像素必須冷到攝氏零下十到二十度；漏電流發熱又會加熱感測器，冷卻不足就會形成熱失控。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Leakage follows T²·exp(−E_eff/(2k_B·T)) and roughly halves for every 7 K of cooling, so inner pixel layers must run at −10 to −20 °C; because the leakage current itself heats the sensor, insufficient cooling leads to thermal runaway.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「漏電流只取決於累積的輻射劑量，與運轉溫度無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Leakage current depends only on accumulated radiation dose, not on operating temperature.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"冷卻板與模組間的導熱膠脫層時，局部溫度升高約 7 K 就讓漏電流加倍，發熱再推高溫度，最終電源電流達上限而跳脫，該模組退出運轉；若偏壓未隨空乏電壓上升而調高，收集電荷持續下降，效率先在最內層崩落。","textEn":"When the thermal adhesive between cooling plate and module delaminates, a local rise of about 7 K doubles the leakage, the extra heat raises temperature further, and the supply eventually hits its current limit and trips, removing the module; if bias is not raised as the depletion voltage climbs, collected charge keeps falling and efficiency collapses first in the innermost layer.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輻射損傷、漏電流與熱失控」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Radiation damage, leakage current and thermal runaway\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的零件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","冷卻板與模組間的導熱膠脫層時，局部溫度升高約 7 K 就讓漏電流加倍，發熱再推高溫度，最終電源電流達上限而跳脫，該模組退出運轉。","解析度就等於像素節距，100 µm 節距不可能量到 10 µm 的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive part first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","When the thermal adhesive between cooling plate and module delaminates, a local rise of about 7 K doubles the leakage, the extra heat raises temperature further, and the supply eventually hits its current limit and trips, removing the module.","Resolution equals the pixel pitch, so a 100 µm pitch cannot measure position to 10 µm."],"answer":1,"explanation":"冷卻板與模組間的導熱膠脫層時，局部溫度升高約 7 K 就讓漏電流加倍，發熱再推高溫度，最終電源電流達上限而跳脫，該模組退出運轉；若偏壓未隨空乏電壓上升而調高，收集電荷持續下降，效率先在最內層崩落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"When the thermal adhesive between cooling plate and module delaminates, a local rise of about 7 K doubles the leakage, the extra heat raises temperature further, and the supply eventually hits its current limit and trips, removing the module; if bias is not raised as the depletion voltage climbs, collected charge keeps falling and efficiency collapses first in the innermost layer. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"a465-v12-s3","title":"量測、校正與誤差預算","titleEn":"Measurement, calibration and error budgets","description":"本階段聚焦「空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束」與「物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams\" and \"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a465-v12-17","title":"空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-16"],"objective":"說明「電荷分享叢集與測試束望遠鏡」如何決定矽像素粒子追蹤器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Charge-sharing cluster and beam telescope” determines the key performance of “Silicon-pixel particle trackers”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"若每顆粒子只點亮一個像素，位置誤差在節距內均勻分佈，解析度為 p/√12；當電荷因 Lorentz 偏移、斜入射或擴散分到兩個像素時，用類比電荷資訊（ADC 或 ToT）做重心或 η 修正內插，解析度可比二元讀出好約三倍。良好的電荷分享需要低門檻與低雜訊，否則邊緣像素的小訊號會被切掉，叢集退化成單像素。驗證解析度需要比待測元件更準的參考，也就是由數層薄 MAPS 組成的測試束望遠鏡。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「電荷分享叢集與測試束望遠鏡」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"If each particle fires only one pixel, the position error is uniformly distributed across the pitch and the resolution is p/√12; when charge is shared between two pixels through Lorentz drift, inclined incidence or diffusion, interpolating with analogue charge (ADC or ToT) by centre of gravity or an eta correction improves on binary readout by about a factor of three. Good sharing requires low threshold and low noise, otherwise the small signal in the edge pixel is cut and the cluster collapses to a single pixel. Verifying resolution needs a reference more precise than the device under test, which is a beam telescope built from several thin MAPS planes. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Charge-sharing cluster and beam telescope”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：二元：σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm（rφ）、150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm（z）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Binary: σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm in rφ and 150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm in z.","failure":"常見誤解：「解析度就等於像素節距，100 µm 節距不可能量到 10 µm 的位置。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Resolution equals the pixel pitch, so a 100 µm pitch cannot measure position to 10 µm.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「電荷分享叢集與測試束望遠鏡」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Charge-sharing cluster and beam telescope”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-17-k1","title":"空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束","titleEn":"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams","text":"若每顆粒子只點亮一個像素，位置誤差在節距內均勻分佈，解析度為 p/√12；當電荷因 Lorentz 偏移、斜入射或擴散分到兩個像素時，用類比電荷資訊（ADC 或 ToT）做重心或 η 修正內插，解析度可比二元讀出好約三倍。良好的電荷分享需要低門檻與低雜訊，否則邊緣像素的小訊號會被切掉，叢集退化成單像素。","textEn":"If each particle fires only one pixel, the position error is uniformly distributed across the pitch and the resolution is p/√12; when charge is shared between two pixels through Lorentz drift, inclined incidence or diffusion, interpolating with analogue charge (ADC or ToT) by centre of gravity or an eta correction improves on binary readout by about a factor of three. Good sharing requires low threshold and low noise, otherwise the small signal in the edge pixel is cut and the cluster collapses to a single pixel.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：解析度就等於像素節距，100 µm 節距不可能量到 10 µm 的位置。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Resolution equals the pixel pitch, so a 100 µm pitch cannot measure position to 10 µm. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams\" is correct?","options":["解析度就等於像素節距，100 µm 節距不可能量到 10 µm 的位置。","像素越小，頂點解析度一定越好，與物質量無關。","若每顆粒子只點亮一個像素，位置誤差在節距內均勻分佈，解析度為 p/√12。"],"optionsEn":["Resolution equals the pixel pitch, so a 100 µm pitch cannot measure position to 10 µm.","Smaller pixels always give better vertex resolution regardless of material.","If each particle fires only one pixel, the position error is uniformly distributed across the pitch and the resolution is p/√12."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若每顆粒子只點亮一個像素，位置誤差在節距內均勻分佈，解析度為 p/√12；當電荷因 Lorentz 偏移、斜入射或擴散分到兩個像素時，用類比電荷資訊（ADC 或 ToT）做重心或 η 修正內插，解析度可比二元讀出好約三倍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"If each particle fires only one pixel, the position error is uniformly distributed across the pitch and the resolution is p/√12; when charge is shared between two pixels through Lorentz drift, inclined incidence or diffusion, interpolating with analogue charge (ADC or ToT) by centre of gravity or an eta correction improves on binary readout by about a factor of three. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"a465-v12-18","title":"空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束：定量估算","titleEn":"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「電荷分享叢集與測試束望遠鏡」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Charge-sharing cluster and beam telescope” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：二元：σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm（rφ）、150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm（z）。利用 Lorentz 分享後 rφ 可達約 10 µm。測試束量得殘差寬度 σ_res = 10.5 µm、望遠鏡外插誤差 σ_tel = 3.0 µm，則 σ_DUT = √(σ_res² − σ_tel²) = √(110.25 − 9) ≈ 10.1 µm；若忽略望遠鏡項，等於把解析度高估約 4%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Binary: σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm in rφ and 150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm in z. With Lorentz sharing, rφ reaches about 10 µm. If the test beam gives a residual width σ_res = 10.5 µm and the telescope extrapolation error is σ_tel = 3.0 µm, then σ_DUT = √(σ_res² − σ_tel²) = √(110.25 − 9) ≈ 10.1 µm; ignoring the telescope term overstates the error by about 4%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：在 DESY 或 CERN SPS 測試束，把待測模組放在 EUDET 型望遠鏡中間，以旋轉台掃描入射角，記錄叢集尺寸與殘差對角度的關係；分別對叢集大小 1、2、3 以上的事件求殘差，確認多數事件為雙像素叢集，並畫像素內效率圖，檢查角落與凸塊附近的效率損失。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At the DESY or CERN SPS test beam, place the module under test in the middle of an EUDET-type telescope, scan the incidence angle on a rotation stage, and record cluster size and residual versus angle; compute residuals separately for cluster sizes 1, 2 and 3 or more, confirm that most events are two-pixel clusters, and map in-pixel efficiency to check for losses at corners and near the bump.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"二元：σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm（rφ）、150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm（z）。利用 Lorentz 分享後 rφ 可達約 10 µm。測試束量得殘差寬度 σ_res = 10.5 µm、望遠鏡外插誤差 σ_tel = 3.0 µm，則 σ_DUT = √(σ_res² − σ_tel²) = √(110.25 − 9) ≈ 10.1 µm；若忽略望遠鏡項，等於把解析度高估約 4%。","textEn":"Binary: σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm in rφ and 150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm in z. With Lorentz sharing, rφ reaches about 10 µm. If the test beam gives a residual width σ_res = 10.5 µm and the telescope extrapolation error is σ_tel = 3.0 µm, then σ_DUT = √(σ_res² − σ_tel²) = √(110.25 − 9) ≈ 10.1 µm; ignoring the telescope term overstates the error by about 4%.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams\", which statement holds?","options":["二元：σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm（rφ）、150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm（z）。","殘差分佈置中且很窄，就代表追蹤器幾何已完全正確。","只要接上偏壓，整片感測器就全部是靈敏區，空乏深度與偏壓無關。"],"optionsEn":["Binary: σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm in rφ and 150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm in z.","Centred, narrow residual distributions prove the tracker geometry is completely correct.","Once bias is applied the whole sensor is sensitive, and depletion depth does not depend on voltage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"二元：σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm（rφ）、150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm（z）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Binary: σ = p/√12 = 100/3.46 ≈ 28.9 µm in rφ and 150/3.46 ≈ 43.3 µm in z. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"a465-v12-19","title":"空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「電荷分享叢集與測試束望遠鏡」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Charge-sharing cluster and beam telescope” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"在 DESY 或 CERN SPS 測試束，把待測模組放在 EUDET 型望遠鏡中間，以旋轉台掃描入射角，記錄叢集尺寸與殘差對角度的關係；分別對叢集大小 1、2、3 以上的事件求殘差，確認多數事件為雙像素叢集，並畫像素內效率圖，檢查角落與凸塊附近的效率損失。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At the DESY or CERN SPS test beam, place the module under test in the middle of an EUDET-type telescope, scan the incidence angle on a rotation stage, and record cluster size and residual versus angle; compute residuals separately for cluster sizes 1, 2 and 3 or more, confirm that most events are two-pixel clusters, and map in-pixel efficiency to check for losses at corners and near the bump. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：照射後電荷收集下降，邊緣像素的分享電荷跌到門檻以下，叢集變小，解析度從約 10 µm 退回接近二元值；若重建仍用照射前的 η 修正表，誤差還會帶有隨入射角變化的系統偏移。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: After irradiation, reduced charge collection pushes the shared charge in edge pixels below threshold, clusters shrink and resolution degrades from about 10 µm towards the binary value; if reconstruction still uses the pre-irradiation eta-correction tables, the error also carries an angle-dependent systematic offset.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在 DESY 或 CERN SPS 測試束，把待測模組放在 EUDET 型望遠鏡中間，以旋轉台掃描入射角，記錄叢集尺寸與殘差對角度的關係；分別對叢集大小 1、2、3 以上的事件求殘差，確認多數事件為雙像素叢集，並畫像素內效率圖，檢查角落與凸塊附近的效率損失。","textEn":"At the DESY or CERN SPS test beam, place the module under test in the middle of an EUDET-type telescope, scan the incidence angle on a rotation stage, and record cluster size and residual versus angle; compute residuals separately for cluster sizes 1, 2 and 3 or more, confirm that most events are two-pixel clusters, and map in-pixel efficiency to check for losses at corners and near the bump.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-19-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在 DESY 或 CERN SPS 測試束，把待測模組放在 EUDET 型望遠鏡中間，以旋轉台掃描入射角，記錄叢集尺寸與殘差對角度的關係。","MAPS 只是把混合式像素做得更薄，輻射硬度與時間解析度完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","At the DESY or CERN SPS test beam, place the module under test in the middle of an EUDET-type telescope, scan the incidence angle on a rotation stage, and record cluster size and residual versus angle.","MAPS are simply thinner hybrid pixels with identical radiation hardness and timing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在 DESY 或 CERN SPS 測試束，把待測模組放在 EUDET 型望遠鏡中間，以旋轉台掃描入射角，記錄叢集尺寸與殘差對角度的關係；分別對叢集大小 1、2、3 以上的事件求殘差，確認多數事件為雙像素叢集，並畫像素內效率圖，檢查角落與凸塊附近的效率損失。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"At the DESY or CERN SPS test beam, place the module under test in the middle of an EUDET-type telescope, scan the incidence angle on a rotation stage, and record cluster size and residual versus angle; compute residuals separately for cluster sizes 1, 2 and 3 or more, confirm that most events are two-pixel clusters, and map in-pixel efficiency to check for losses at corners and near the bump. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"a465-v12-20","title":"空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束：失效診斷","titleEn":"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「電荷分享叢集與測試束望遠鏡」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Charge-sharing cluster and beam telescope” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"照射後電荷收集下降，邊緣像素的分享電荷跌到門檻以下，叢集變小，解析度從約 10 µm 退回接近二元值；若重建仍用照射前的 η 修正表，誤差還會帶有隨入射角變化的系統偏移。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"After irradiation, reduced charge collection pushes the shared charge in edge pixels below threshold, clusters shrink and resolution degrades from about 10 µm towards the binary value; if reconstruction still uses the pre-irradiation eta-correction tables, the error also carries an angle-dependent systematic offset. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：驗證解析度需要比待測元件更準的參考，也就是由數層薄 MAPS 組成的測試束望遠鏡。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Verifying resolution needs a reference more precise than the device under test, which is a beam telescope built from several thin MAPS planes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「解析度就等於像素節距，100 µm 節距不可能量到 10 µm 的位置。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Resolution equals the pixel pitch, so a 100 µm pitch cannot measure position to 10 µm.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"照射後電荷收集下降，邊緣像素的分享電荷跌到門檻以下，叢集變小，解析度從約 10 µm 退回接近二元值；若重建仍用照射前的 η 修正表，誤差還會帶有隨入射角變化的系統偏移。","textEn":"After irradiation, reduced charge collection pushes the shared charge in edge pixels below threshold, clusters shrink and resolution degrades from about 10 µm towards the binary value; if reconstruction still uses the pre-irradiation eta-correction tables, the error also carries an angle-dependent systematic offset.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空間解析度：節距、電荷分享與測試束」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Spatial resolution: pitch, charge sharing and test beams\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","像素越小，頂點解析度一定越好，與物質量無關。","照射後電荷收集下降，邊緣像素的分享電荷跌到門檻以下，叢集變小，解析度從約 10 µm 退回接近二元值。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Smaller pixels always give better vertex resolution regardless of material.","After irradiation, reduced charge collection pushes the shared charge in edge pixels below threshold, clusters shrink and resolution degrades from about 10 µm towards the binary value."],"answer":2,"explanation":"照射後電荷收集下降，邊緣像素的分享電荷跌到門檻以下，叢集變小，解析度從約 10 µm 退回接近二元值；若重建仍用照射前的 η 修正表，誤差還會帶有隨入射角變化的系統偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"After irradiation, reduced charge collection pushes the shared charge in edge pixels below threshold, clusters shrink and resolution degrades from about 10 µm towards the binary value; if reconstruction still uses the pre-irradiation eta-correction tables, the error also carries an angle-dependent systematic offset. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"a465-v12-21","title":"物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-20"],"objective":"說明「每層物質量與束管」如何決定矽像素粒子追蹤器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Per-layer material and beam pipe” determines the key performance of “Silicon-pixel particle trackers”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"追蹤器每一層的矽、讀出晶片、冷卻管、碳纖維支撐與電纜都會讓粒子發生多重庫侖散射，散射角寬度依 Highland 公式與 √(x/X₀) 成正比、與動量成反比。低動量粒子的撞擊參數與頂點解析度通常由物質量而非像素解析度決定，所以內層設計的競賽是降低 X/X₀ 並縮小第一層半徑；只有在高動量時才回到幾何項，由命中解析度與層間槓桿臂決定。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「每層物質量與束管」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Every layer's silicon, readout chips, cooling pipes, carbon-fibre supports and cables cause multiple Coulomb scattering, with an angular width that by the Highland formula scales as √(x/X₀) and inversely with momentum. For low-momentum particles the impact-parameter and vertex resolution is usually set by material rather than by pixel resolution, so inner-layer design becomes a contest to cut X/X₀ and shrink the first-layer radius; only at high momentum does the geometric term, set by hit resolution and the lever arm between layers, dominate again. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Per-layer material and beam pipe”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)]。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)].","failure":"常見誤解：「像素越小，頂點解析度一定越好，與物質量無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Smaller pixels always give better vertex resolution regardless of material.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「每層物質量與束管」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Per-layer material and beam pipe”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-21-k1","title":"物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數","titleEn":"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter","text":"追蹤器每一層的矽、讀出晶片、冷卻管、碳纖維支撐與電纜都會讓粒子發生多重庫侖散射，散射角寬度依 Highland 公式與 √(x/X₀) 成正比、與動量成反比。低動量粒子的撞擊參數與頂點解析度通常由物質量而非像素解析度決定，所以內層設計的競賽是降低 X/X₀ 並縮小第一層半徑；只有在高動量時才回到幾何項，由命中解析度與層間槓桿臂決定。","textEn":"Every layer's silicon, readout chips, cooling pipes, carbon-fibre supports and cables cause multiple Coulomb scattering, with an angular width that by the Highland formula scales as √(x/X₀) and inversely with momentum. For low-momentum particles the impact-parameter and vertex resolution is usually set by material rather than by pixel resolution, so inner-layer design becomes a contest to cut X/X₀ and shrink the first-layer radius; only at high momentum does the geometric term, set by hit resolution and the lever arm between layers, dominate again.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：像素越小，頂點解析度一定越好，與物質量無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Smaller pixels always give better vertex resolution regardless of material. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter\" is correct?","options":["追蹤器每一層的矽、讀出晶片、冷卻管、碳纖維支撐與電纜都會讓粒子發生多重庫侖散射，散射角寬度依 Highland 公式與 √(x/X₀) 成正比、與動量成反比。","像素越小，頂點解析度一定越好，與物質量無關。","感測器效率 99.9%，整個像素系統的效率就是 99.9%。"],"optionsEn":["Every layer's silicon, readout chips, cooling pipes, carbon-fibre supports and cables cause multiple Coulomb scattering, with an angular width that by the Highland formula scales as √(x/X₀) and inversely with momentum.","Smaller pixels always give better vertex resolution regardless of material.","If the sensor is 99.9% efficient, the whole pixel system is 99.9% efficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"追蹤器每一層的矽、讀出晶片、冷卻管、碳纖維支撐與電纜都會讓粒子發生多重庫侖散射，散射角寬度依 Highland 公式與 √(x/X₀) 成正比、與動量成反比。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Every layer's silicon, readout chips, cooling pipes, carbon-fibre supports and cables cause multiple Coulomb scattering, with an angular width that by the Highland formula scales as √(x/X₀) and inversely with momentum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"a465-v12-22","title":"物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數：定量估算","titleEn":"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「每層物質量與束管」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Per-layer material and beam pipe” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)]。x/X₀ = 1.0%、p = 1 GeV/c：θ₀ ≈ 1.12 mrad，在 r₁ = 29 mm 的第一層貢獻 ≈ 29 mm × 1.12 mrad ≈ 33 µm。兩層幾何項 σ·√(r₁² + r₂²)/(r₂ − r₁)，σ = 10 µm、r₂ = 68 mm 得 19 µm；合計 √(33² + 19²) ≈ 38 µm。若每層降到 0.35% X₀，θ₀ ≈ 0.63 mrad，合計約 26 µm；在 10 GeV/c 時散射項只剩 3 µm，總和約 19 µm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)]. For x/X₀ = 1.0% and p = 1 GeV/c, θ₀ ≈ 1.12 mrad, contributing ≈ 29 mm × 1.12 mrad ≈ 33 µm at a first layer of radius r₁ = 29 mm. The two-layer geometric term σ·√(r₁² + r₂²)/(r₂ − r₁) with σ = 10 µm and r₂ = 68 mm gives 19 µm, for a total of √(33² + 19²) ≈ 38 µm. Cutting each layer to 0.35% X₀ gives θ₀ ≈ 0.63 mrad and a total near 26 µm; at 10 GeV/c the scattering term is only 3 µm and the total is about 19 µm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以光子轉換頂點與強子交互作用頂點的空間分佈做物質層析，把重建頂點密度換算成 X/X₀ 對半徑與偽快度的分佈，與幾何模擬的物質量逐區比較；另把撞擊參數解析度對 p_T 的曲線擬合成 a ⊕ b/p_T，a 對應幾何項、b 對應散射項，與設計值比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use the spatial distribution of photon-conversion and hadronic-interaction vertices as material tomography, converting vertex density into X/X₀ versus radius and pseudorapidity and comparing region by region with the simulated geometry; fit the impact-parameter resolution versus p_T as a ⊕ b/p_T, where a is the geometric term and b the scattering term, and compare both with the design.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)]。x/X₀ = 1.0%、p = 1 GeV/c：θ₀ ≈ 1.12 mrad，在 r₁ = 29 mm 的第一層貢獻 ≈ 29 mm × 1.12 mrad ≈ 33 µm。兩層幾何項 σ·√(r₁² + r₂²)/(r₂ − r₁)，σ = 10 µm、r₂ = 68 mm 得 19 µm；合計 √(33² + 19²) ≈ 38 µm。若每層降到 0.35% X₀，θ₀ ≈ 0.63 mrad，合計約 26 µm；在 10 GeV/c 時散射項只剩 3 µm，總和約 19 µm。","textEn":"θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)]. For x/X₀ = 1.0% and p = 1 GeV/c, θ₀ ≈ 1.12 mrad, contributing ≈ 29 mm × 1.12 mrad ≈ 33 µm at a first layer of radius r₁ = 29 mm. The two-layer geometric term σ·√(r₁² + r₂²)/(r₂ − r₁) with σ = 10 µm and r₂ = 68 mm gives 19 µm, for a total of √(33² + 19²) ≈ 38 µm. Cutting each layer to 0.35% X₀ gives θ₀ ≈ 0.63 mrad and a total near 26 µm; at 10 GeV/c the scattering term is only 3 µm and the total is about 19 µm.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter\", which statement holds?","options":["每顆穿過像素的粒子都產生同樣多的電子，訊號是固定值。","θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)]。","MAPS 只是把混合式像素做得更薄，輻射硬度與時間解析度完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Every particle crossing a pixel frees the same number of electrons, so the signal is fixed.","θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)].","MAPS are simply thinner hybrid pixels with identical radiation hardness and timing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)]。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"θ₀ = (13.6 MeV/p)·√(x/X₀)·[1 + 0.038 ln(x/X₀)]. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"a465-v12-23","title":"物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「每層物質量與束管」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Per-layer material and beam pipe” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以光子轉換頂點與強子交互作用頂點的空間分佈做物質層析，把重建頂點密度換算成 X/X₀ 對半徑與偽快度的分佈，與幾何模擬的物質量逐區比較；另把撞擊參數解析度對 p_T 的曲線擬合成 a ⊕ b/p_T，a 對應幾何項、b 對應散射項，與設計值比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use the spatial distribution of photon-conversion and hadronic-interaction vertices as material tomography, converting vertex density into X/X₀ versus radius and pseudorapidity and comparing region by region with the simulated geometry; fit the impact-parameter resolution versus p_T as a ⊕ b/p_T, where a is the geometric term and b the scattering term, and compare both with the design. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：模擬漏算冷卻液、連接器或電纜，實際物質量多出 20 到 30%，低 p_T 軌跡的誤差被低估，軌跡 χ² 分佈偏寬，b 夸克標記的效率與誤判率偏離模擬，使物理分析帶入未被察覺的系統誤差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Simulation that omits coolant, connectors or cables underestimates material by 20 to 30%, so low-p_T track errors are underestimated, track χ² distributions broaden, and b-tagging efficiency and mistag rates drift from simulation, injecting unnoticed systematics into physics analyses.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以光子轉換頂點與強子交互作用頂點的空間分佈做物質層析，把重建頂點密度換算成 X/X₀ 對半徑與偽快度的分佈，與幾何模擬的物質量逐區比較；另把撞擊參數解析度對 p_T 的曲線擬合成 a ⊕ b/p_T，a 對應幾何項、b 對應散射項，與設計值比對。","textEn":"Use the spatial distribution of photon-conversion and hadronic-interaction vertices as material tomography, converting vertex density into X/X₀ versus radius and pseudorapidity and comparing region by region with the simulated geometry; fit the impact-parameter resolution versus p_T as a ⊕ b/p_T, where a is the geometric term and b the scattering term, and compare both with the design.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-23-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter\"?","options":["只要模擬結果看起來合理，就可以省略實體量測與校正。","漏電流只取決於累積的輻射劑量，與運轉溫度無關。","以光子轉換頂點與強子交互作用頂點的空間分佈做物質層析，把重建頂點密度換算成 X/X₀ 對半徑與偽快度的分佈，與幾何模擬的物質量逐區比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the simulation looks reasonable, physical measurement and calibration can be skipped.","Leakage current depends only on accumulated radiation dose, not on operating temperature.","Use the spatial distribution of photon-conversion and hadronic-interaction vertices as material tomography, converting vertex density into X/X₀ versus radius and pseudorapidity and comparing region by region with the simulated geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以光子轉換頂點與強子交互作用頂點的空間分佈做物質層析，把重建頂點密度換算成 X/X₀ 對半徑與偽快度的分佈，與幾何模擬的物質量逐區比較；另把撞擊參數解析度對 p_T 的曲線擬合成 a ⊕ b/p_T，a 對應幾何項、b 對應散射項，與設計值比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use the spatial distribution of photon-conversion and hadronic-interaction vertices as material tomography, converting vertex density into X/X₀ versus radius and pseudorapidity and comparing region by region with the simulated geometry; fit the impact-parameter resolution versus p_T as a ⊕ b/p_T, where a is the geometric term and b the scattering term, and compare both with the design. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"a465-v12-24","title":"物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「每層物質量與束管」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Per-layer material and beam pipe” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"模擬漏算冷卻液、連接器或電纜，實際物質量多出 20 到 30%，低 p_T 軌跡的誤差被低估，軌跡 χ² 分佈偏寬，b 夸克標記的效率與誤判率偏離模擬，使物理分析帶入未被察覺的系統誤差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Simulation that omits coolant, connectors or cables underestimates material by 20 to 30%, so low-p_T track errors are underestimated, track χ² distributions broaden, and b-tagging efficiency and mistag rates drift from simulation, injecting unnoticed systematics into physics analyses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：低動量粒子的撞擊參數與頂點解析度通常由物質量而非像素解析度決定，所以內層設計的競賽是降低 X/X₀ 並縮小第一層半徑；只有在高動量時才回到幾何項，由命中解析度與層間槓桿臂決定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: For low-momentum particles the impact-parameter and vertex resolution is usually set by material rather than by pixel resolution, so inner-layer design becomes a contest to cut X/X₀ and shrink the first-layer radius; only at high momentum does the geometric term, set by hit resolution and the lever arm between layers, dominate again.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「像素越小，頂點解析度一定越好，與物質量無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Smaller pixels always give better vertex resolution regardless of material.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"模擬漏算冷卻液、連接器或電纜，實際物質量多出 20 到 30%，低 p_T 軌跡的誤差被低估，軌跡 χ² 分佈偏寬，b 夸克標記的效率與誤判率偏離模擬，使物理分析帶入未被察覺的系統誤差。","textEn":"Simulation that omits coolant, connectors or cables underestimates material by 20 to 30%, so low-p_T track errors are underestimated, track χ² distributions broaden, and b-tagging efficiency and mistag rates drift from simulation, injecting unnoticed systematics into physics analyses.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「物質量 X/X₀、多重散射與撞擊參數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Material budget X/X₀, multiple scattering and impact parameter\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["模擬漏算冷卻液、連接器或電纜，實際物質量多出 20 到 30%，低 p_T 軌跡的誤差被低估，軌跡 χ² 分佈偏寬，b 夸克標記的效率與誤判率偏離模擬，使物理分析帶入未被察覺的系統誤差。","只要重新開機或重設軟體，硬體失效也會一併排除。","感測器效率 99.9%，整個像素系統的效率就是 99.9%。"],"optionsEn":["Simulation that omits coolant, connectors or cables underestimates material by 20 to 30%, so low-p_T track errors are underestimated, track χ² distributions broaden, and b-tagging efficiency and mistag rates drift from simulation, injecting unnoticed systematics into physics analyses.","Restarting or resetting the software also clears hardware failures.","If the sensor is 99.9% efficient, the whole pixel system is 99.9% efficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"模擬漏算冷卻液、連接器或電纜，實際物質量多出 20 到 30%，低 p_T 軌跡的誤差被低估，軌跡 χ² 分佈偏寬，b 夸克標記的效率與誤判率偏離模擬，使物理分析帶入未被察覺的系統誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Simulation that omits coolant, connectors or cables underestimates material by 20 to 30%, so low-p_T track errors are underestimated, track χ² distributions broaden, and b-tagging efficiency and mistag rates drift from simulation, injecting unnoticed systematics into physics analyses. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"a465-v12-s4","title":"系統整合、驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Integration, validation and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬」與「軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth\" and \"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a465-v12-25","title":"命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-24"],"objective":"說明「雙欄緩衝與資料鏈路」如何決定矽像素粒子追蹤器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Double-column buffers and data links” determines the key performance of “Silicon-pixel particle trackers”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"內層像素的命中率大致隨半徑按 1/r² 增加，在高亮度下達每平方公分數百 MHz。觸發式讀出必須把每個命中保留到第一級觸發決定到來（CMS 約 4 µs），讀出晶片以雙欄為單位暫存時間戳記與電荷，緩衝滿了新命中就遺失；被觸發的事件再經串列鏈路送出，鏈路頻寬決定可承受的觸發率。因此系統效率損失不只來自感測器，也來自數位架構的死時間與緩衝溢位。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「雙欄緩衝與資料鏈路」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Inner-layer hit rates rise roughly as 1/r² with radius, reaching hundreds of MHz per square centimetre at high luminosity. Triggered readout must hold every hit until the first-level trigger decision arrives, about 4 µs at CMS; the readout chip buffers timestamps and charge per double column and loses new hits once the buffer is full, and triggered events then leave over serial links whose bandwidth sets the sustainable trigger rate. System inefficiency therefore comes not only from the sensor but also from dead time and buffer overflow in the digital architecture. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Double-column buffers and data links”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：假設命中率 200 MHz/cm²（教學值）、像素 100×150 µm²：每次束團交叉每像素佔用率 = 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume 200 MHz/cm² (teaching value) and 100×150 µm² pixels: the per-pixel occupancy per bunch crossing is 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴.","failure":"常見誤解：「感測器效率 99.9%，整個像素系統的效率就是 99.9%。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the sensor is 99.9% efficient, the whole pixel system is 99.9% efficient.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「雙欄緩衝與資料鏈路」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Double-column buffers and data links”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-25-k1","title":"命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬","titleEn":"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth","text":"內層像素的命中率大致隨半徑按 1/r² 增加，在高亮度下達每平方公分數百 MHz。觸發式讀出必須把每個命中保留到第一級觸發決定到來（CMS 約 4 µs），讀出晶片以雙欄為單位暫存時間戳記與電荷，緩衝滿了新命中就遺失；被觸發的事件再經串列鏈路送出，鏈路頻寬決定可承受的觸發率。","textEn":"Inner-layer hit rates rise roughly as 1/r² with radius, reaching hundreds of MHz per square centimetre at high luminosity. Triggered readout must hold every hit until the first-level trigger decision arrives, about 4 µs at CMS; the readout chip buffers timestamps and charge per double column and loses new hits once the buffer is full, and triggered events then leave over serial links whose bandwidth sets the sustainable trigger rate.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：感測器效率 99.9%，整個像素系統的效率就是 99.9%。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the sensor is 99.9% efficient, the whole pixel system is 99.9% efficient. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth\" is correct?","options":["感測器效率 99.9%，整個像素系統的效率就是 99.9%。","內層像素的命中率大致隨半徑按 1/r² 增加，在高亮度下達每平方公分數百 MHz。","殘差分佈置中且很窄，就代表追蹤器幾何已完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["If the sensor is 99.9% efficient, the whole pixel system is 99.9% efficient.","Inner-layer hit rates rise roughly as 1/r² with radius, reaching hundreds of MHz per square centimetre at high luminosity.","Centred, narrow residual distributions prove the tracker geometry is completely correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"內層像素的命中率大致隨半徑按 1/r² 增加，在高亮度下達每平方公分數百 MHz。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Inner-layer hit rates rise roughly as 1/r² with radius, reaching hundreds of MHz per square centimetre at high luminosity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"a465-v12-26","title":"命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬：定量估算","titleEn":"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙欄緩衝與資料鏈路」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Double-column buffers and data links” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：假設命中率 200 MHz/cm²（教學值）、像素 100×150 µm²：每次束團交叉每像素佔用率 = 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴。一個 160 像素的雙欄（0.024 cm²）命中率 4.8 MHz，4 µs 延遲內平均暫存 19.2 筆；依 Poisson 分佈，32 格緩衝的溢位機率約 0.26%，24 格則約 11.6%。每顆 0.62 cm² 讀出晶片每次交叉 3.1 個命中，100 kHz 觸發、每命中 24 bit 約 7.5 Mbit/s，尚不含標頭。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume 200 MHz/cm² (teaching value) and 100×150 µm² pixels: the per-pixel occupancy per bunch crossing is 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴. A 160-pixel double column (0.024 cm²) sees 4.8 MHz and holds on average 19.2 hits during a 4 µs latency; by Poisson statistics a 32-slot buffer overflows with probability about 0.26% and a 24-slot buffer about 11.6%. Each 0.62 cm² readout chip sees 3.1 hits per crossing, so a 100 kHz trigger at 24 bits per hit needs about 7.5 Mbit/s before headers. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以 X 光管或高強度束流在不同命中率下量效率，畫效率對命中率曲線並與 Poisson 緩衝模型比較；運轉時監控觸發後的命中數、鏈路錯誤計數與 FIFO 滿旗標，確認在設計亮度下由緩衝與死時間造成的效率損失低於 1%。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure efficiency at several hit rates with an X-ray tube or high-intensity beam and compare the efficiency-versus-rate curve with the Poisson buffer model; during operation monitor hits per trigger, link error counters and FIFO-full flags, confirming that buffer and dead-time losses stay below 1% at design luminosity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"假設命中率 200 MHz/cm²（教學值）、像素 100×150 µm²：每次束團交叉每像素佔用率 = 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴。一個 160 像素的雙欄（0.024 cm²）命中率 4.8 MHz，4 µs 延遲內平均暫存 19.2 筆；依 Poisson 分佈，32 格緩衝的溢位機率約 0.26%，24 格則約 11.6%。每顆 0.62 cm² 讀出晶片每次交叉 3.1 個命中，100 kHz 觸發、每命中 24 bit 約 7.5 Mbit/s，尚不含標頭。","textEn":"Assume 200 MHz/cm² (teaching value) and 100×150 µm² pixels: the per-pixel occupancy per bunch crossing is 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴. A 160-pixel double column (0.024 cm²) sees 4.8 MHz and holds on average 19.2 hits during a 4 µs latency; by Poisson statistics a 32-slot buffer overflows with probability about 0.26% and a 24-slot buffer about 11.6%. Each 0.62 cm² readout chip sees 3.1 hits per crossing, so a 100 kHz trigger at 24 bits per hit needs about 7.5 Mbit/s before headers.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth\", which statement holds?","options":["只要接上偏壓，整片感測器就全部是靈敏區，空乏深度與偏壓無關。","漏電流只取決於累積的輻射劑量，與運轉溫度無關。","假設命中率 200 MHz/cm²（教學值）、像素 100×150 µm²：每次束團交叉每像素佔用率 = 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴。"],"optionsEn":["Once bias is applied the whole sensor is sensitive, and depletion depth does not depend on voltage.","Leakage current depends only on accumulated radiation dose, not on operating temperature.","Assume 200 MHz/cm² (teaching value) and 100×150 µm² pixels: the per-pixel occupancy per bunch crossing is 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設命中率 200 MHz/cm²（教學值）、像素 100×150 µm²：每次束團交叉每像素佔用率 = 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume 200 MHz/cm² (teaching value) and 100×150 µm² pixels: the per-pixel occupancy per bunch crossing is 2×10⁸ × 25×10⁻⁹ × 1.5×10⁻⁴ ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁴. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"a465-v12-27","title":"命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「雙欄緩衝與資料鏈路」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Double-column buffers and data links” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以 X 光管或高強度束流在不同命中率下量效率，畫效率對命中率曲線並與 Poisson 緩衝模型比較；運轉時監控觸發後的命中數、鏈路錯誤計數與 FIFO 滿旗標，確認在設計亮度下由緩衝與死時間造成的效率損失低於 1%。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure efficiency at several hit rates with an X-ray tube or high-intensity beam and compare the efficiency-versus-rate curve with the Poisson buffer model; during operation monitor hits per trigger, link error counters and FIFO-full flags, confirming that buffer and dead-time losses stay below 1% at design luminosity. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：亮度提高後最內層的雙欄緩衝溢位，效率下降數個百分比，且損失集中在高佔用率、高堆疊的事件，造成與亮度相關的系統偏差；這正是高亮度升級時讀出晶片要加大緩衝並改用高速數位鏈路的主要理由之一。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: As luminosity rises the innermost double-column buffers overflow and efficiency drops by several percent, concentrated in high-occupancy, high-pile-up events, creating a luminosity-dependent bias; this is one of the main reasons high-luminosity upgrades enlarge readout-chip buffers and move to fast digital links.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以 X 光管或高強度束流在不同命中率下量效率，畫效率對命中率曲線並與 Poisson 緩衝模型比較；運轉時監控觸發後的命中數、鏈路錯誤計數與 FIFO 滿旗標，確認在設計亮度下由緩衝與死時間造成的效率損失低於 1%。","textEn":"Measure efficiency at several hit rates with an X-ray tube or high-intensity beam and compare the efficiency-versus-rate curve with the Poisson buffer model; during operation monitor hits per trigger, link error counters and FIFO-full flags, confirming that buffer and dead-time losses stay below 1% at design luminosity.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-27-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth\"?","options":["以 X 光管或高強度束流在不同命中率下量效率，畫效率對命中率曲線並與 Poisson 緩衝模型比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","解析度就等於像素節距，100 µm 節距不可能量到 10 µm 的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Measure efficiency at several hit rates with an X-ray tube or high-intensity beam and compare the efficiency-versus-rate curve with the Poisson buffer model.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Resolution equals the pixel pitch, so a 100 µm pitch cannot measure position to 10 µm."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以 X 光管或高強度束流在不同命中率下量效率，畫效率對命中率曲線並與 Poisson 緩衝模型比較；運轉時監控觸發後的命中數、鏈路錯誤計數與 FIFO 滿旗標，確認在設計亮度下由緩衝與死時間造成的效率損失低於 1%。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure efficiency at several hit rates with an X-ray tube or high-intensity beam and compare the efficiency-versus-rate curve with the Poisson buffer model; during operation monitor hits per trigger, link error counters and FIFO-full flags, confirming that buffer and dead-time losses stay below 1% at design luminosity. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"a465-v12-28","title":"命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙欄緩衝與資料鏈路」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Double-column buffers and data links” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"亮度提高後最內層的雙欄緩衝溢位，效率下降數個百分比，且損失集中在高佔用率、高堆疊的事件，造成與亮度相關的系統偏差；這正是高亮度升級時讀出晶片要加大緩衝並改用高速數位鏈路的主要理由之一。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"As luminosity rises the innermost double-column buffers overflow and efficiency drops by several percent, concentrated in high-occupancy, high-pile-up events, creating a luminosity-dependent bias; this is one of the main reasons high-luminosity upgrades enlarge readout-chip buffers and move to fast digital links. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：因此系統效率損失不只來自感測器，也來自數位架構的死時間與緩衝溢位。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: System inefficiency therefore comes not only from the sensor but also from dead time and buffer overflow in the digital architecture.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「感測器效率 99.9%，整個像素系統的效率就是 99.9%。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the sensor is 99.9% efficient, the whole pixel system is 99.9% efficient.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"亮度提高後最內層的雙欄緩衝溢位，效率下降數個百分比，且損失集中在高佔用率、高堆疊的事件，造成與亮度相關的系統偏差；這正是高亮度升級時讀出晶片要加大緩衝並改用高速數位鏈路的主要理由之一。","textEn":"As luminosity rises the innermost double-column buffers overflow and efficiency drops by several percent, concentrated in high-occupancy, high-pile-up events, creating a luminosity-dependent bias; this is one of the main reasons high-luminosity upgrades enlarge readout-chip buffers and move to fast digital links.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「命中率、觸發延遲緩衝與讀出頻寬」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hit rate, trigger-latency buffering and readout bandwidth\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","亮度提高後最內層的雙欄緩衝溢位，效率下降數個百分比，且損失集中在高佔用率、高堆疊的事件，造成與亮度相關的系統偏差。","殘差分佈置中且很窄，就代表追蹤器幾何已完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","As luminosity rises the innermost double-column buffers overflow and efficiency drops by several percent, concentrated in high-occupancy, high-pile-up events, creating a luminosity-dependent bias.","Centred, narrow residual distributions prove the tracker geometry is completely correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"亮度提高後最內層的雙欄緩衝溢位，效率下降數個百分比，且損失集中在高佔用率、高堆疊的事件，造成與亮度相關的系統偏差；這正是高亮度升級時讀出晶片要加大緩衝並改用高速數位鏈路的主要理由之一。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"As luminosity rises the innermost double-column buffers overflow and efficiency drops by several percent, concentrated in high-occupancy, high-pile-up events, creating a luminosity-dependent bias; this is one of the main reasons high-luminosity upgrades enlarge readout-chip buffers and move to fast digital links. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"a465-v12-29","title":"軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-28"],"objective":"說明「軌跡殘差與對準參數」如何決定矽像素粒子追蹤器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Track residuals and alignment parameters” determines the key performance of “Silicon-pixel particle trackers”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"安裝後模組位置只知道到數十微米，遠差於約 10 µm 的命中解析度，所以最終幾何由大量軌跡決定：把每個模組的三個平移與三個轉動當作參數，與軌跡參數一起最小化殘差 χ²，例如 Millepede-II 的全域擬合。某些整體變形如扭轉、伸縮與弓形，讓所有軌跡仍然擬合良好卻系統性地偏移動量，稱為弱模態，只能靠宇宙射線、束暈軌跡或 Z→μμ 質量約束打破。試運轉交接必須包含幾何版本、Lorentz 角、門檻與遮罩像素表以及對準驗證圖。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「軌跡殘差與對準參數」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After installation module positions are known only to tens of micrometres, far worse than the roughly 10 µm hit resolution, so the final geometry is determined from many tracks: each module's three translations and three rotations become parameters minimised together with track parameters in a residual χ², for example in a Millepede-II global fit. Certain global deformations such as twist, telescope and bowing leave every track well fitted yet bias momentum systematically; these weak modes are broken only with cosmic rays, beam-halo tracks or Z→μμ mass constraints. The commissioning handoff must include the geometry version, Lorentz angle, thresholds and masked-pixel tables, and alignment validation plots. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Track residuals and alignment parameters”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：每模組統計精度約 σ_hit/√N：σ_hit = 10 µm，要達 1 µm 需約 100 條穿越軌跡（再乘幾何因子）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Per-module statistical precision is about σ_hit/√N: with σ_hit = 10 µm, reaching 1 µm needs about 100 crossing tracks, times a geometric factor.","failure":"常見誤解：「殘差分佈置中且很窄，就代表追蹤器幾何已完全正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Centred, narrow residual distributions prove the tracker geometry is completely correct.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「軌跡殘差與對準參數」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Track residuals and alignment parameters”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-29-k1","title":"軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接","titleEn":"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff","text":"安裝後模組位置只知道到數十微米，遠差於約 10 µm 的命中解析度，所以最終幾何由大量軌跡決定：把每個模組的三個平移與三個轉動當作參數，與軌跡參數一起最小化殘差 χ²，例如 Millepede-II 的全域擬合。某些整體變形如扭轉、伸縮與弓形，讓所有軌跡仍然擬合良好卻系統性地偏移動量，稱為弱模態，只能靠宇宙射線、束暈軌跡或 Z→μμ 質量約束打破。","textEn":"After installation module positions are known only to tens of micrometres, far worse than the roughly 10 µm hit resolution, so the final geometry is determined from many tracks: each module's three translations and three rotations become parameters minimised together with track parameters in a residual χ², for example in a Millepede-II global fit. Certain global deformations such as twist, telescope and bowing leave every track well fitted yet bias momentum systematically; these weak modes are broken only with cosmic rays, beam-halo tracks or Z→μμ mass constraints.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：殘差分佈置中且很窄，就代表追蹤器幾何已完全正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Centred, narrow residual distributions prove the tracker geometry is completely correct. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff\" is correct?","options":["殘差分佈置中且很窄，就代表追蹤器幾何已完全正確。","每顆穿過像素的粒子都產生同樣多的電子，訊號是固定值。","安裝後模組位置只知道到數十微米，遠差於約 10 µm 的命中解析度，所以最終幾何由大量軌跡決定：把每個模組的三個平移與三個轉動當作參數，與軌跡參數一起最小化殘差 χ²，例如 Millepede-II 的全域擬合。"],"optionsEn":["Centred, narrow residual distributions prove the tracker geometry is completely correct.","Every particle crossing a pixel frees the same number of electrons, so the signal is fixed.","After installation module positions are known only to tens of micrometres, far worse than the roughly 10 µm hit resolution, so the final geometry is determined from many tracks: each module's three translations and three rotations become parameters minimised together with track parameters in a residual χ², for example in a Millepede-II global fit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"安裝後模組位置只知道到數十微米，遠差於約 10 µm 的命中解析度，所以最終幾何由大量軌跡決定：把每個模組的三個平移與三個轉動當作參數，與軌跡參數一起最小化殘差 χ²，例如 Millepede-II 的全域擬合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After installation module positions are known only to tens of micrometres, far worse than the roughly 10 µm hit resolution, so the final geometry is determined from many tracks: each module's three translations and three rotations become parameters minimised together with track parameters in a residual χ², for example in a Millepede-II global fit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"a465-v12-30","title":"軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「軌跡殘差與對準參數」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Track residuals and alignment parameters” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：每模組統計精度約 σ_hit/√N：σ_hit = 10 µm，要達 1 µm 需約 100 條穿越軌跡（再乘幾何因子）。CMS 追蹤器約 17,000 個模組 × 6 自由度 ≈ 10⁵ 個參數。弓高 s = L²/(8R)，R = p_T/(0.3B)：p_T = 45 GeV/c、B = 3.8 T 得 R ≈ 39.5 m；L = 1.1 m 時 s ≈ 3.8 mm，10 µm 的系統弓高偏差造成約 0.26% 的動量偏差，且正負電荷方向相反。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Per-module statistical precision is about σ_hit/√N: with σ_hit = 10 µm, reaching 1 µm needs about 100 crossing tracks, times a geometric factor. The CMS tracker's roughly 17,000 modules × 6 degrees of freedom give about 10⁵ parameters. Sagitta s = L²/(8R) with R = p_T/(0.3B): p_T = 45 GeV/c and B = 3.8 T give R ≈ 39.5 m, and L = 1.1 m gives s ≈ 3.8 mm, so a 10 µm systematic sagitta bias shifts momentum by about 0.26%, with opposite sign for opposite charges. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：畫各模組殘差中位數的分佈（DMR），對準後寬度應遠小於命中解析度；把宇宙射線分成上下兩半各自重建並比較軌跡參數差；檢查 Z→μμ 重建質量對方位角、偽快度與電荷的相依性以找出弱模態；交接文件列出幾何版本、偏壓與溫度、門檻與遮罩表及上述驗證圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot the distribution of per-module median residuals (DMR), whose width after alignment should be far below the hit resolution; split cosmic-ray tracks into upper and lower halves, reconstruct each, and compare track-parameter differences; check the dependence of the reconstructed Z→μμ mass on azimuth, pseudorapidity and charge to expose weak modes; the handoff document lists geometry version, bias and temperature, thresholds and mask tables, and these validation plots.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"每模組統計精度約 σ_hit/√N：σ_hit = 10 µm，要達 1 µm 需約 100 條穿越軌跡（再乘幾何因子）。CMS 追蹤器約 17,000 個模組 × 6 自由度 ≈ 10⁵ 個參數。弓高 s = L²/(8R)，R = p_T/(0.3B)：p_T = 45 GeV/c、B = 3.8 T 得 R ≈ 39.5 m；L = 1.1 m 時 s ≈ 3.8 mm，10 µm 的系統弓高偏差造成約 0.26% 的動量偏差，且正負電荷方向相反。","textEn":"Per-module statistical precision is about σ_hit/√N: with σ_hit = 10 µm, reaching 1 µm needs about 100 crossing tracks, times a geometric factor. The CMS tracker's roughly 17,000 modules × 6 degrees of freedom give about 10⁵ parameters. Sagitta s = L²/(8R) with R = p_T/(0.3B): p_T = 45 GeV/c and B = 3.8 T give R ≈ 39.5 m, and L = 1.1 m gives s ≈ 3.8 mm, so a 10 µm systematic sagitta bias shifts momentum by about 0.26%, with opposite sign for opposite charges.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff\", which statement holds?","options":["每模組統計精度約 σ_hit/√N：σ_hit = 10 µm，要達 1 µm 需約 100 條穿越軌跡（再乘幾何因子）。","MAPS 只是把混合式像素做得更薄，輻射硬度與時間解析度完全相同。","解析度就等於像素節距，100 µm 節距不可能量到 10 µm 的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Per-module statistical precision is about σ_hit/√N: with σ_hit = 10 µm, reaching 1 µm needs about 100 crossing tracks, times a geometric factor.","MAPS are simply thinner hybrid pixels with identical radiation hardness and timing.","Resolution equals the pixel pitch, so a 100 µm pitch cannot measure position to 10 µm."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每模組統計精度約 σ_hit/√N：σ_hit = 10 µm，要達 1 µm 需約 100 條穿越軌跡（再乘幾何因子）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Per-module statistical precision is about σ_hit/√N: with σ_hit = 10 µm, reaching 1 µm needs about 100 crossing tracks, times a geometric factor. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"a465-v12-31","title":"軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「軌跡殘差與對準參數」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Track residuals and alignment parameters” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"畫各模組殘差中位數的分佈（DMR），對準後寬度應遠小於命中解析度；把宇宙射線分成上下兩半各自重建並比較軌跡參數差；檢查 Z→μμ 重建質量對方位角、偽快度與電荷的相依性以找出弱模態；交接文件列出幾何版本、偏壓與溫度、門檻與遮罩表及上述驗證圖。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot the distribution of per-module median residuals (DMR), whose width after alignment should be far below the hit resolution; split cosmic-ray tracks into upper and lower halves, reconstruct each, and compare track-parameter differences; check the dependence of the reconstructed Z→μμ mass on azimuth, pseudorapidity and charge to expose weak modes; the handoff document lists geometry version, bias and temperature, thresholds and mask tables, and these validation plots. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：只用對撞軌跡對準時殘差看起來完美，卻殘留扭轉弱模態，使正負電荷的動量出現相反偏差，μ⁺ 與 μ⁻ 的質量峰錯開；熱循環或磁場開關後若未重做對準，模組數微米的位移也會讓撞擊參數解析度悄悄變差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Aligning with collision tracks alone can give perfect-looking residuals while leaving a twist weak mode that biases positive and negative momenta in opposite directions and separates the μ⁺ and μ⁻ mass peaks; if alignment is not redone after thermal cycles or magnet ramps, module shifts of a few micrometres silently degrade impact-parameter resolution.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫各模組殘差中位數的分佈（DMR），對準後寬度應遠小於命中解析度；把宇宙射線分成上下兩半各自重建並比較軌跡參數差；檢查 Z→μμ 重建質量對方位角、偽快度與電荷的相依性以找出弱模態；交接文件列出幾何版本、偏壓與溫度、門檻與遮罩表及上述驗證圖。","textEn":"Plot the distribution of per-module median residuals (DMR), whose width after alignment should be far below the hit resolution; split cosmic-ray tracks into upper and lower halves, reconstruct each, and compare track-parameter differences; check the dependence of the reconstructed Z→μμ mass on azimuth, pseudorapidity and charge to expose weak modes; the handoff document lists geometry version, bias and temperature, thresholds and mask tables, and these validation plots.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-31-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","畫各模組殘差中位數的分佈（DMR），對準後寬度應遠小於命中解析度。","像素越小，頂點解析度一定越好，與物質量無關。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Plot the distribution of per-module median residuals (DMR), whose width after alignment should be far below the hit resolution.","Smaller pixels always give better vertex resolution regardless of material."],"answer":1,"explanation":"畫各模組殘差中位數的分佈（DMR），對準後寬度應遠小於命中解析度；把宇宙射線分成上下兩半各自重建並比較軌跡參數差；檢查 Z→μμ 重建質量對方位角、偽快度與電荷的相依性以找出弱模態；交接文件列出幾何版本、偏壓與溫度、門檻與遮罩表及上述驗證圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot the distribution of per-module median residuals (DMR), whose width after alignment should be far below the hit resolution; split cosmic-ray tracks into upper and lower halves, reconstruct each, and compare track-parameter differences; check the dependence of the reconstructed Z→μμ mass on azimuth, pseudorapidity and charge to expose weak modes; the handoff document lists geometry version, bias and temperature, thresholds and mask tables, and these validation plots. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"a465-v12-32","title":"軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"prerequisiteIds":["a465-v12-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「軌跡殘差與對準參數」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Track residuals and alignment parameters” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"只用對撞軌跡對準時殘差看起來完美，卻殘留扭轉弱模態，使正負電荷的動量出現相反偏差，μ⁺ 與 μ⁻ 的質量峰錯開；熱循環或磁場開關後若未重做對準，模組數微米的位移也會讓撞擊參數解析度悄悄變差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Aligning with collision tracks alone can give perfect-looking residuals while leaving a twist weak mode that biases positive and negative momenta in opposite directions and separates the μ⁺ and μ⁻ mass peaks; if alignment is not redone after thermal cycles or magnet ramps, module shifts of a few micrometres silently degrade impact-parameter resolution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：試運轉交接必須包含幾何版本、Lorentz 角、門檻與遮罩像素表以及對準驗證圖。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The commissioning handoff must include the geometry version, Lorentz angle, thresholds and masked-pixel tables, and alignment validation plots.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「殘差分佈置中且很窄，就代表追蹤器幾何已完全正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Centred, narrow residual distributions prove the tracker geometry is completely correct.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a465-v12-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用對撞軌跡對準時殘差看起來完美，卻殘留扭轉弱模態，使正負電荷的動量出現相反偏差，μ⁺ 與 μ⁻ 的質量峰錯開；熱循環或磁場開關後若未重做對準，模組數微米的位移也會讓撞擊參數解析度悄悄變差。","textEn":"Aligning with collision tracks alone can give perfect-looking residuals while leaving a twist weak mode that biases positive and negative momenta in opposite directions and separates the μ⁺ and μ⁻ mass peaks; if alignment is not redone after thermal cycles or magnet ramps, module shifts of a few micrometres silently degrade impact-parameter resolution.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]},{"id":"a465-v12-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軌跡式對準、弱模態與試運轉交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Track-based alignment, weak modes and commissioning handoff\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","每顆穿過像素的粒子都產生同樣多的電子，訊號是固定值。","只用對撞軌跡對準時殘差看起來完美，卻殘留扭轉弱模態，使正負電荷的動量出現相反偏差，μ⁺ 與 μ⁻ 的質量峰錯開。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","Every particle crossing a pixel frees the same number of electrons, so the signal is fixed.","Aligning with collision tracks alone can give perfect-looking residuals while leaving a twist weak mode that biases positive and negative momenta in opposite directions and separates the μ⁺ and μ⁻ mass peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只用對撞軌跡對準時殘差看起來完美，卻殘留扭轉弱模態，使正負電荷的動量出現相反偏差，μ⁺ 與 μ⁻ 的質量峰錯開；熱循環或磁場開關後若未重做對準，模組數微米的位移也會讓撞擊參數解析度悄悄變差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Aligning with collision tracks alone can give perfect-looking residuals while leaving a twist weak mode that biases positive and negative momenta in opposite directions and separates the μ⁺ and μ⁻ mass peaks; if alignment is not redone after thermal cycles or magnet ramps, module shifts of a few micrometres silently degrade impact-parameter resolution. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4}],"sourceIds":["v12o-cms-pixel-production-commissioning","v12o-alice-its2-performance","v12o-cern-alice-ls2-media-kit","v12o-psi-cms-pixel-press"],"curriculumVersion":12,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":800}};
